1
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:22,980
=Weekend Crush=

2
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:24,440
We're here, babe.

3
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:25,020
Okay.

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:26,080
(3:35AM, Sunrise Lookout, Beijing)

5
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:26,920
Come on. Let's catch the sunrise.

6
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:27,640
Are you cold?

7
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:28,920
Want my jacket?

8
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:29,600
You wear it.

9
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:30,280
I'm not cold.

10
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:34,040
This is nice. Really nice.

11
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:34,880
The view's pretty amazing.

12
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:35,680
Seriously nice.

13
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:43,540
(Filmed by Zhao Xilun)

14
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:44,320
Are you cold?

15
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:45,280
Here, put this on.

16
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:47,200
(Puts on Zhao Xilun's jacket)

17
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,440
That actually looks great on you.

18
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:50,240
Like a ghost girl?

19
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,400
More like a CEO.

20
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:54,220
(Filmed by Zhao Xilun)

21
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:55,560
There you go, smiling again.

22
00:00:57,880 --> 00:00:59,040
Now you're winking at me, too.

23
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:00,320
I don't know.

24
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:01,720
You brought out my Xinjiang accent.

25
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:02,320
Winking at me.

26
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:05,800
Should we sit over here?

27
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:06,360
Sure.

28
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:08,040
I'll grab you a blanket.

29
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:09,280
I saw one over here.

30
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:12,960
(Grabs bug spray)

31
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:14,200
Let me spray some on you.

32
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:17,780
(So thoughtful)

33
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:20,460
(Checking)

34
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:23,060
(Grabs a blanket)

35
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:23,960
Here, cover up.

36
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:24,920
Okay.

37
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:25,680
Are you cold?

38
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:27,040
No, I'm really not.

39
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:28,400
I'll tell you if I get cold.

40
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:29,240
(Hands it over)
Okay.

41
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:33,200
Thanks.

42
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:40,440
Happy birthday.

43
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:41,240
Thank you.

44
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:44,120
Honestly,

45
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:45,320
when we first started hanging out,

46
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:47,440
I had no idea you were this thoughtful.

47
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:49,000
When did you realize?

48
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,520
I think it was that time

49
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:53,760
when I mentioned

50
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:54,960
how well

51
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:55,560
you take care of others.

52
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:58,360
I think it was in the kitchen.

53
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:01,200
How hot do you want your water?

54
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:04,280
Hot, but not too hot to drink.

55
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:07,240
400 mL at 85°C,

56
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:09,760
plus 100 mL at 25°C.

57
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:11,160
That comes to around 70°C.

58
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,760
Perfect.

59
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:22,960
It's flapping against my leg.

60
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:23,480
Let's move.

61
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:24,360
Let's sit over there.

62
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:24,960
Okay.

63
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:27,840
Thanks.

64
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:31,800
Want another spray of bug repellent?

65
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:32,600
(Checking on her)
No, I'm good.

66
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:34,120
Let me check.

67
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:36,680
What time's sunrise?

68
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:38,400
It still says 5:01AM.

69
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,160
What time is it now?

70
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:40,120
4AM.

71
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,200
One more hour.

72
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:43,160
The sun should come up over there.

73
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,020
Whoa.

74
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:44,880
It's getting brighter already.

75
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:45,720
Yeah, so fast.

76
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:47,220
(Where the sun will rise)

77
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:50,520
I can't really use my hand right now.

78
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:51,960
Can you grab something for me?

79
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:53,640
I've got this...

80
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:56,000
thing for watching the sunrise

81
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,040
in the trunk.

82
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:57,920
Really?

83
00:02:57,920 --> 00:02:58,920
Can you open it for me?

84
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,000
Wait, I think I see something.

85
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:12,160
Today is our...

86
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:13,800
one-month anniversary.

87
00:03:14,820 --> 00:03:17,820
(Happy Birthday)

88
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:18,660
Oh my God!

89
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,040
Happy anniversary, babe.

90
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:21,320
Okay!

91
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:23,540
(Happy anniversary, babe!)

92
00:03:28,630 --> 00:03:29,300
Wow!

93
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:30,040
It's beautiful!

94
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,320
This is why I was late.

95
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:34,280
And these are...

96
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:36,320
the flowers I arranged for you.

97
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:39,120
(Handmade arrangement)
These are the earrings you wore.

98
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:41,200
And this book

99
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,720
is from the first time we talked alone

100
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:44,320
in the Signal House's library.

101
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:45,280
And this is you, my queen.

102
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:47,010
Wow.

103
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:50,700
(Before heading out)

104
00:04:02,510 --> 00:04:04,030
Oh my God.

105
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,600
I figured these flowers

106
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:08,280
would last a little longer.

107
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:09,080
They definitely will.

108
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:12,240
Thank you.

109
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:16,240
Happy birthday, babe.

110
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:16,920
Thank you.

111
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,140
(Happy birthday!)

112
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:25,890
Wow!

113
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:26,600
There's more?

114
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:27,560
Can I pick this up now?

115
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:28,120
Go ahead.

116
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:29,320
Yeah.

117
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:31,110
Wow!

118
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,880
This one looks like a painting.

119
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:34,720
This is from when we were in Thailand.

120
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:35,280
I know.

121
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:39,240
Isn't that the photo I sent you?

122
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:44,640
Happy birthday.

123
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:47,880
Thank you.

124
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:50,320
I'm so happy. Seriously.

125
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:51,960
And happy anniversary, too.

126
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:53,400
(One month together)
Yeah, happy anniversary.

127
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:56,160
Our anniversary
is right by your birthday.

128
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:56,840
Exactly.

129
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:58,840
And then, early this morning,

130
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,120
you said you wanted to see the sunrise.

131
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:01,080
I was really excited

132
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:03,320
because the timing worked out perfectly.

133
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:05,400
It's perfect.

134
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:06,360
I just wanted

135
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:08,280
to make your birthday unforgettable.

136
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:10,120
Because I'll be leaving for school

137
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,640
in two months.

138
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:12,600
And I just...

139
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:17,560
I'll miss you.

140
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:20,240
I'll miss you, too.

141
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,600
Should we unwrap the cake?

142
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:32,360
Let's do it.

143
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:36,840
You can actually pull this cake apart.

144
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:40,280
Happy anniversary!

145
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:41,400
It's melted a little, though.

146
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:44,160
(Happy anniversary)
It's okay. You can still read it.

147
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:46,420
Wow.

148
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:48,040
You really put so much thought
into this.

149
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:53,680
I love it.

150
00:05:56,520 --> 00:05:57,560
Make a wish.

151
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:58,840
You do it.

152
00:05:58,840 --> 00:05:59,640
Okay.

153
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:02,540
(Holding hands)

154
00:06:07,810 --> 00:06:08,580
Okay, I'm blowing them out.

155
00:06:08,580 --> 00:06:09,010
Go for it!

156
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:11,780
It'll definitely come true.

157
00:06:11,780 --> 00:06:12,920
(It'll definitely come true)

158
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:13,720
It will.

159
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:18,800
I can't bring myself to cut into it.

160
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:21,600
Let's keep the "Happy Anniversary" part.

161
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:25,960
Wow.

162
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:27,800
It's getting light out.

163
00:06:31,230 --> 00:06:32,000
Whoa.

164
00:06:32,070 --> 00:06:33,160
Look at that sunrise glow.

165
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,960
It looks like a volcano erupting.

166
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:52,280
Have you ever watched the sunrise?

167
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:55,240
I think this is the first time

168
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,450
I've ever gone out of my way to see it.

169
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:58,060
Yeah, same here.

170
00:06:58,070 --> 00:07:00,040
It's my first time getting up
to watch the sunrise.

171
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:01,840
Honestly, coming out here together

172
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:03,280
means more than the sunrise itself.

173
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:06,560
(The journey matters more than the sunrise)
The sun rises every day.

174
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:07,800
But watching it together,

175
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:09,200
on a day this special?

176
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:11,640
That's something rare.

177
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:12,640
Yeah.

178
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:14,880
That's why I was so nervous

179
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:17,240
about whether it'd be cloudy today.

180
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:19,560
Clouds or no clouds, I'm happy.

181
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:20,580
As long as I'm with you.

182
00:07:20,590 --> 00:07:21,660
That's all I need, too.

183
00:07:21,660 --> 00:07:23,140
(As long as we're together)

184
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:24,720
So beautiful.

185
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:27,040
You can see the whole city from here.

186
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:28,320
Yeah.

187
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:35,360
Remember what I told you
in the stargazing room?

188
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:39,040
I wanted to see the other side of you.

189
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:42,000
It was just how I imagined it,

190
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,720
only even better.

191
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:48,720
That's why I said

192
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:51,880
we should take time
to get to know each other.

193
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:54,640
It helps me picture our future.

194
00:07:56,580 --> 00:07:59,000
How does that work?

195
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,120
Well...

196
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:02,960
The little things you do

197
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:05,040
show me what you're like

198
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:07,560
and what being together might look like.

199
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:09,680
And what do you picture?

200
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:13,320
A happy future together, of course.

201
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:14,680
Of course.

202
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:15,940
(A happy future together. Of course)

203
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,840
I'll be back before you know it.

204
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:21,720
I just need to finish grad school.

205
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:22,280
Okay.

206
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:24,040
Let's both stay happy, okay?

207
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,680
Yeah, you too.

208
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:29,000
And let's video call a lot.

209
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:34,480
And see each other often.

210
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:39,200
I'll be back before you know it.

211
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:40,120
You better hurry back.

212
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:40,920
I will.

213
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,600
We're only 22.

214
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:45,480
But I really hope

215
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,360
I can give you a future
you can count on.

216
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:48,960
That shows you're someone
who takes commitment seriously.

217
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,270
Is that the sun?

218
00:09:06,270 --> 00:09:07,440
(Peeking out)

219
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,480
It really is the sun.

220
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:10,440
Wow!

221
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:13,160
I thought we were out of luck today.

222
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,760
This is my first time...

223
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:17,520
(First time catching the sunrise)

224
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,240
Seriously!

225
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:23,780
(Filmed by Zhao Xilun)

226
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,120
The sun's coming up!

227
00:09:25,650 --> 00:09:26,400
Wow!

228
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:28,640
We actually caught the sunrise!

229
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:29,600
It's gorgeous.

230
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,640
We're so lucky!

231
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:31,560
Yeah.

232
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:32,400
It's all thanks to you

233
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:34,280
that we got so lucky.

234
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:35,080
Thanks to both of us.

235
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:37,200
(Thanks to both of us)

236
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:39,000
Because today

237
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,120
is our one-month anniversary

238
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,320
and your birthday.

239
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:42,840
Thank you, sunshine.

240
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:44,600
Wow!

241
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:46,960
It's slowly peeking over the horizon.

242
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:47,900
Wow!

243
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:50,840
It feels like everything's falling
into place.

244
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:51,200
It does.

245
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,760
I can't even find the words.

246
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:57,120
I'm getting a little emotional.

247
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:59,400
I'm just really moved.

248
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,080
You're tearing up again.

249
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:03,920
I can't help it. I'm emotional.

250
00:10:03,920 --> 00:10:06,360
I was so worried it'd be cloudy today.

251
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,920
I guess the universe saw
how much you cared.

252
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:12,720
(How much we both cared)

253
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:13,920
Nope, how much we both cared.

254
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:40,820
(Mushrooms. Entrance)

255
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:43,160
We can find mushrooms
up in the mountains.

256
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:44,360
So we can pick mushrooms?

257
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:45,160
Yeah.

258
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:47,480
Let's look for mushrooms.

259
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:48,280
Then we'll cook.

260
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:49,000
Okay.

261
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,600
The mushrooms I showed you earlier.

262
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:50,880
Okay.

263
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:51,920
We have all of those
up in the mountains.

264
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:52,320
Okay.

265
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,520
It's just a little hill here.

266
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:56,800
Once we get over two hills,

267
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:58,000
we'll reach a flat path.

268
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:58,800
Okay.

269
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:00,680
Are the rocks hurting your heels?

270
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:02,340
How about I give you a piggyback ride?

271
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:03,020
(Concerned)

272
00:11:03,020 --> 00:11:03,280
Sure.

273
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:04,080
I'll carry you on my back.

274
00:11:04,730 --> 00:11:05,720
Can you hold this for me?

275
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:07,400
It's hard for her to walk
in those shoes.

276
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:08,920
They're rubbing against my feet.

277
00:11:10,590 --> 00:11:12,280
Can you carry me?

278
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:16,440
No.

279
00:11:17,770 --> 00:11:18,520
Can you carry me?

280
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:19,120
I can.

281
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:19,920
Okay.

282
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:21,180
(Picks her up)

283
00:11:22,540 --> 00:11:23,540
(Holds on)

284
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:25,440
Are you tired?

285
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:26,200
Not at all.

286
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:27,000
Okay.

287
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:31,920
Let's start picking mushrooms.

288
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:33,680
They're so easy to spot.

289
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:36,000
Do we just pick them by hand?

290
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:36,240
Yeah.

291
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:36,960
It's fine to pick them by hand.

292
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:38,320
There are ants.

293
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:42,960
This one.

294
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,240
Yeah.

295
00:11:45,230 --> 00:11:46,440
Is this one a mushroom?

296
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:47,600
Is it a mushroom?

297
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:48,400
No, that one's not.

298
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:49,640
Oh, it's not?

299
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:51,120
It probably fell from a tree.

300
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,520
Maybe it's a chestnut.

301
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,640
Look at them from a distance.

302
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:57,240
They look like
a whole bunch of mushrooms.

303
00:12:00,240 --> 00:12:01,120
Those are all mushrooms.

304
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:05,600
You've never picked mushrooms before,
have you?

305
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:06,560
No.

306
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:09,240
This is my first time doing this.

307
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:12,240
That's great! You get

308
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:13,480
to experience this first with me.

309
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:14,680
(Sharing a first in life together)

310
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:15,560
This one's a mushroom.

311
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:16,960
This one?

312
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:17,760
Yeah.

313
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:18,840
This one's a good one.

314
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:19,880
This one's edible.

315
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:23,120
Over here.

316
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:23,480
Where?

317
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:24,280
There's one here.

318
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,280
This is a porcini mushroom.

319
00:12:26,340 --> 00:12:27,340
(It's also known as white porcini
or six-legged mushroom)

320
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:28,180
(A fungus in the Boletaceae family)
It's delicious.

321
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:28,720
This one's tasty.

322
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:29,800
I think this one tastes really good.

323
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:30,920
Careful.

324
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,360
Here, hold on to me.

325
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:36,360
There's one here.

326
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:37,280
Yeah.

327
00:12:37,280 --> 00:12:38,080
Can we eat this one?

328
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:38,800
Yes, it's edible.

329
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:39,880
This is a green-cracking russula.

330
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:40,680
Green-cracking russula?

331
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:41,480
Yeah.

332
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:41,940
(Officially known as Russula virescens)

333
00:12:41,940 --> 00:12:42,550
(A fungus in the Russulaceae family
and Russula genus)

334
00:12:42,550 --> 00:12:42,950
(It mostly grows in mixed forests)

335
00:12:42,950 --> 00:12:43,480
(Its flesh is white, thick, and crisp)

336
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:44,060
(It's a rare wild edible mushroom)

337
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:45,480
I'm kinda afraid

338
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:46,400
to touch it.

339
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:47,760
This one.

340
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,480
Its scientific name
is wrinkled-cap bolete.

341
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:52,200
(It's also known as the yellow bolete)

342
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:53,600
(Boletaceae family, Rugiboletus genus)
It looks terrifying.

343
00:12:53,620 --> 00:12:54,800
(It grows in mixed forests)
Try picking it and see how it feels.

344
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:56,680
I'll give it a try.

345
00:12:57,820 --> 00:12:59,580
(Grunting with effort)

346
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:02,000
This feels pretty satisfying!

347
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:06,320
(Harvesting mushrooms)
It's so yellow!

348
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:09,600
Have you found any other mushrooms?

349
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:11,240
Look at our giant mushroom.

350
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:12,360
We'll share some with you.

351
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:12,800
It's huge.

352
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:13,480
Take this yellow one.

353
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:14,040
It's so big.

354
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:16,200
You have so many yellow ones.

355
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:17,200
They smell amazing. Take a sniff.

356
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:17,840
Oh my gosh.

357
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:20,120
(Sniffing)

358
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:21,520
Put it in your basket. It's fine.

359
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:23,320
Take another one. There's plenty more.

360
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:24,520
Well, I won't say no to that.

361
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:25,320
Here you go.

362
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:29,080
Go look for some big mushrooms.

363
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:30,240
Okay.

364
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,240
No rush. Let's take our time.

365
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:38,200
You did so well.

366
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:41,080
Slow down.

367
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:41,920
There's a branch here.

368
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:46,820
(Spots something exciting)

369
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:47,680
There's a huge mushroom here.

370
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:48,520
A huge mushroom.

371
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:51,760
This seems pretty nice.

372
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:55,440
Let's head over there and take a look.

373
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:56,200
Okay.

374
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:57,600
Watch your head.

375
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:58,900
(Always looking out for her)
Okay.

376
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:01,520
There are thorns.

377
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:03,520
Come down.

378
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:05,800
It's right here.

379
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:07,560
It should be buried in here.

380
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:09,640
You have sharp eyes.

381
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:14,800
Two, even.

382
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:17,080
Slow down a little.

383
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:20,360
Guess what this is called.

384
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:22,520
(Joking)
This is an oyster mushroom.

385
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:24,200
I was thinking the same thing.

386
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:25,000
Right?

387
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:26,840
Stay here.

388
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:27,280
I'll go first.

389
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:27,920
I'll look out for you.

390
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:31,280
Let's go.

391
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:32,520
(Protecting her head)
Watch out for the rocks.

392
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,440
I feel like the farther out we go,

393
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:37,560
the bigger the mushrooms get.

394
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:39,800
Would you dare touch it?

395
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:40,900
(Sunflower)
Of course I would.

396
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:41,900
(Teasing)

397
00:14:42,660 --> 00:14:44,100
(Punches)

398
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:46,580
(Keeps teasing)

399
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:54,200
What are you doing?

400
00:14:57,760 --> 00:14:58,720
Don't scare me.

401
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,560
- I can't handle being scared.
- There's a bug.

402
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:01,520
I really can't handle that.

403
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:03,640
It's pretty funny, this thing.

404
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:05,240
It's actually kind of fun.

405
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:08,240
Let's go rest by the kitchen.

406
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:08,800
There's water.

407
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:09,600
Sure.

408
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:13,520
I'll get you a wet wipe
and clean your feet.

409
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:14,320
Okay.

410
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:16,480
You've been walking...

411
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:17,200
My foot's rubbed raw.

412
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:18,840
It's a little raw.

413
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:19,280
Yeah.

414
00:15:19,280 --> 00:15:20,520
Is this spot rubbed raw?

415
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:22,860
(Gently wiping)

416
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,840
(Worried)
Be honest. Does it sting?

417
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:26,840
A little. It stings a bit.

418
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:27,960
It still stings quite a bit.

419
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:28,800
But it's fine now that you've wiped it.

420
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:29,400
It stings quite a bit.

421
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:37,780
(Carefully)

422
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:39,440
Anywhere else besides this spot?

423
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:40,520
Is it this spot?

424
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:41,880
And this one.

425
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:42,720
This spot here.

426
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:44,520
What's going on?

427
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:45,560
You're back already.

428
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:46,360
Yeah.

429
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:48,600
Did you guys go far?

430
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:49,600
Not as far as you guys did.

431
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:50,440
We didn't climb as high.

432
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:52,400
Are your shoes hurting your feet?

433
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:53,080
Yeah.

434
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:54,120
It rubbed her skin raw.

435
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,200
The front of your foot?

436
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:55,760
Yeah.

437
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:57,200
You're okay, right?

438
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:58,880
Yeah, my shoes are pretty comfortable.

439
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:03,060
(Hands over a tissue)

440
00:16:03,060 --> 00:16:04,200
Wipe your face.

441
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:05,320
I'm fine.

442
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:06,640
I didn't even sweat.

443
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:08,440
Does it sting?

444
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:09,280
This spot stings a little.

445
00:16:09,280 --> 00:16:10,080
It stings a bit.

446
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:11,920
What about lower down?

447
00:16:11,920 --> 00:16:12,760
That part's fine.

448
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:18,400
We'll cook in a little while.

449
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:19,360
Sure.

450
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:24,680
The lobster tails...

451
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:25,840
Here, let me find them for you.

452
00:16:25,840 --> 00:16:26,360
Okay.

453
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:27,920
Si.

454
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:30,200
Is there a seasoning packet in that bag?

455
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:30,680
Yeah.

456
00:16:30,980 --> 00:16:32,600
(Seasoning prepared in advance)
Are you making crawfish now?

457
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,440
Here.

458
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:35,440
Thanks.

459
00:16:35,770 --> 00:16:36,640
(Ingredients prepared in advance)
Thanks.

460
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:37,680
You're so thoughtful.

461
00:16:37,680 --> 00:16:39,080
Are all the seasonings over there?

462
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:39,600
Yeah.

463
00:16:40,260 --> 00:16:41,540
(Today's ingredients)

464
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:43,020
(Prepping the ingredients)

465
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:47,220
(Scoring the chicken wings)

466
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:52,340
(Patting the ribs dry)

467
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:03,100
(Still prepping ingredients)

468
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:03,840
Let's bring them

469
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:04,600
some water.

470
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:06,560
They probably wanted some ice water.

471
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:07,600
Pour some for them.

472
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:08,720
Pour him a little more.

473
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:10,050
(Resupplying the crew)
I think that's too much.

474
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:11,680
Here's the ice water.

475
00:17:13,340 --> 00:17:16,580
(Drinking)

476
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:21,440
Finished?

477
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:23,920
The cat's here to hang out
with you guys.

478
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:24,760
Have you had some water?

479
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:25,560
This is ice water.

480
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:26,360
Have you had any?

481
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:28,480
Did you get some?

482
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:30,600
Yeah, I did.

483
00:17:30,600 --> 00:17:32,000
Are you making iron-pot stew?

484
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,360
I'll make the stew first.

485
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:33,960
It'll take a little while.

486
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:36,960
Are you making chicken wings?

487
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:37,520
Yeah.

488
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:38,680
The chef's cooking.

489
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:41,040
(Wu Xingying's POV)

490
00:17:41,040 --> 00:17:42,080
He's making iron-pot stew.

491
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:45,800
I don't know if it'll taste good.

492
00:17:45,800 --> 00:17:46,800
It's my first time ever making it.

493
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:47,560
First time.

494
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:49,240
Well, we'll all give it a try in a bit.

495
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:52,060
(Filming the chef at the same time)

496
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:55,000
This kind of reminds me of Signal House.

497
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:55,760
Right?

498
00:17:56,420 --> 00:17:57,540
(Moving closer)

499
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:01,240
Let me take a photo of you
from this angle.

500
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:02,960
Stand up straighter.

501
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:04,600
Straighter.

502
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:05,900
(Standing up straight)

503
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,120
This cat is so well-behaved.

504
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:11,680
Even the cat came looking for you.

505
00:18:14,580 --> 00:18:15,820
(Recording)

506
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:21,880
We could take it from this angle.

507
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:26,840
(Wu Xingying's POV)
Let's see

508
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:28,720
what these two chefs are cooking up.

509
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:31,280
Can't wait to try it.

510
00:18:32,280 --> 00:18:33,680
Whose "star" is this?

511
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:35,560
(Laughing)
Whose "star" is this?

512
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:36,600
Yours.

513
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:39,600
My "star" can cook.

514
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:41,120
Who else could I belong to?

515
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,360
Definitely not anyone else's.

516
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:43,400
I can't belong to anyone else?

517
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:44,120
Nope.

518
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:45,840
Then you're my "star" too.

519
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,760
You're my "star" too.

520
00:18:47,860 --> 00:18:50,300
(Happy)

521
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:52,880
Let's see what the chef cooks up.

522
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:54,800
Don't get your hopes up.

523
00:18:56,120 --> 00:18:57,000
If you don't expect much,

524
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,080
you won't be disappointed.

525
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:00,960
Ready to go?

526
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:02,440
Are we cooking over there now?

527
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:03,120
Yeah.

528
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:04,120
They have pots and stuff over there.

529
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:11,480
Give it to me.

530
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:11,960
I'll take one for you.

531
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:12,890
(Helping)
It's okay.

532
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:14,120
No, it's slippery. Take it slow.

533
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,000
It's fine. It's not slippery.

534
00:19:18,120 --> 00:19:19,320
I knew one would fall.

535
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:23,960
I hope I can
do these ingredients justice.

536
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:25,680
As long as it doesn't taste bad.

537
00:19:26,340 --> 00:19:27,020
(Ingredients prepared by Sun Bohan:
Pork ribs)

538
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:27,740
(Ingredients prepared by Cui Yihang:
Chicken)

539
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:31,000
There's quite a few steps.

540
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,100
(Looking up the recipe online)

541
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:33,640
This looks a little tricky.

542
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:35,800
Yeah. I won't remember it all.

543
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:36,360
Right?

544
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:37,880
How about I walk you through it
step by step?

545
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:39,320
First, let it simmer.

546
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:40,400
It needs to simmer for 40 minutes.

547
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:41,560
That long?

548
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:44,200
You're already sweating.

549
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:46,380
(Wiping sweat)
Let me wipe that off for you.

550
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:47,160
I'm fine.

551
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:49,040
(Wiping)
The challenge makes it worth it.

552
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:55,360
What are you making?

553
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:56,720
Coconut curry chicken.

554
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:00,420
(Feeding)

555
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:06,680
You like carrots?

556
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:10,080
Because they're healthy, like fruit.

557
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:11,880
You like eating healthy fruit.

558
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:14,880
Let me see
how to get this firewood burning.

559
00:20:16,080 --> 00:20:17,640
I can just light it like this, right?

560
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:27,220
(Hmm?)

561
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:35,160
Light the front.

562
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:35,960
Smoke's coming out of the front.

563
00:20:35,960 --> 00:20:36,840
The front.

564
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:37,360
Yeah.

565
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:38,140
(Finally lit)

566
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:41,460
(Not convinced)

567
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:42,480
This.

568
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:43,440
You need to wait a bit.

569
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:44,880
Those two pieces of wood
aren't going to catch.

570
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:46,080
(Too little firewood)
Two pieces won't do it.

571
00:20:46,080 --> 00:20:47,400
Why don't you turn it off first?
Let's switch places.

572
00:20:49,100 --> 00:20:51,180
(Firewood rescue)

573
00:20:52,760 --> 00:20:53,800
Be careful.

574
00:20:55,540 --> 00:20:57,260
(Finally lit)

575
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:01,860
(Getting the fire going)

576
00:21:03,180 --> 00:21:04,420
(Adding butter)

577
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:08,060
(Heating oil in the pan)

578
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:11,020
(Not wasting a drop,
and looking elegant)

579
00:21:12,940 --> 00:21:17,060
(Coating the pan evenly)

580
00:21:18,740 --> 00:21:21,180
(Cui Yihang's first dish:
Coconut curry chicken)

581
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:24,480
(Adding onions and tomatoes)

582
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:26,480
Do you want a stronger flavor, or...

583
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:27,640
A richer flavor is fine.

584
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:28,680
A little richer.

585
00:21:29,060 --> 00:21:31,380
(Adjusting the flavor)

586
00:21:31,420 --> 00:21:34,260
(Adding potatoes, carrots, and chicken)

587
00:21:34,280 --> 00:21:35,440
Now we just let it cook.

588
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:36,040
Right.

589
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,480
Let me check the first step.

590
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:40,360
I kind of forgot.

591
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:41,080
(Reviewing the recipe)

592
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:42,040
Stir-fry the vegetables first.

593
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:43,600
Have you already prepped them?

594
00:21:43,600 --> 00:21:44,440
Everything's ready.

595
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:45,600
Add a spoonful of oil first.

596
00:21:46,080 --> 00:21:47,160
Coat the pan thoroughly.

597
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,680
(Helping pour in the oil)

598
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:49,360
Okay.

599
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:55,600
Add the vegetables.

600
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:58,820
(Sun Bohan's first dish: Iron-pot stew)

601
00:21:58,840 --> 00:22:00,240
Turn the heat up high
and keep stir-frying.

602
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:02,860
(Knowing what he's doing)

603
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:05,480
Take them out
when the green beans turn bright green.

604
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:05,800
Okay.

605
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:07,520
You got it, boss.

606
00:22:07,520 --> 00:22:08,320
Alright.

607
00:22:09,760 --> 00:22:10,720
Bright green.

608
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:14,720
Take them out
when they turn bright green, right?

609
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:15,160
Right.

610
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:16,280
But why does the corn

611
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:17,160
look burnt?

612
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:18,280
I think it's burning a little.

613
00:22:18,340 --> 00:22:19,900
(Burnt?)

614
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:23,400
Let's put them in a bowl.

615
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:24,760
Careful.

616
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:25,640
There's a fire right next to you.

617
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:26,640
(Concerned)

618
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:27,640
Is there too...

619
00:22:27,640 --> 00:22:28,880
Is there too little oil or too much?

620
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:30,480
I think there might not be enough oil.

621
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:31,580
This wok is too big.

622
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:32,380
(The wok takes all the blame)

623
00:22:32,720 --> 00:22:33,920
Yeah, it's too big.

624
00:22:36,500 --> 00:22:40,380
(Adding the pork ribs)

625
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:41,840
Stir-fry for two or three minutes

626
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:42,800
until they're lightly golden.

627
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:44,760
Then pour the cooking wine
along the edge of the pan.

628
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:46,400
Add the thirteen-spice seasoning,
soybean paste, and light soy sauce.

629
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:49,040
Thirteen-spice seasoning
and five-spice powder.

630
00:22:49,040 --> 00:22:50,140
(Adding seasonings)

631
00:22:51,020 --> 00:22:53,700
(Continuing to stir-fry over high heat)

632
00:22:53,720 --> 00:22:54,880
I think you can take them out now.

633
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:55,840
Okay.

634
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:03,520
They're burnt.

635
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:05,440
But they look so appetizing.

636
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:07,040
I actually like them this way.

637
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:08,960
I like them burnt black.

638
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:11,120
You're so good at cheering me up.

639
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:13,400
Look at them.
Don't they look appetizing?

640
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:16,640
We both

641
00:23:16,640 --> 00:23:17,760
like them burnt.

642
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:18,920
What kind of meat is this?

643
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:19,200
Pork ribs.

644
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:19,400
It's fine.

645
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:20,120
I like them burnt too.

646
00:23:20,120 --> 00:23:21,280
I love it when they're a little charred.

647
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:23,440
Really?

648
00:23:23,800 --> 00:23:24,160
Yeah.

649
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:25,760
Yours looks so appetizing.

650
00:23:25,760 --> 00:23:27,000
It's okay. Don't be nervous.

651
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:27,840
This is normal.

652
00:23:27,840 --> 00:23:29,360
(Comforting)
It's tricky to cook. Don't worry.

653
00:23:29,360 --> 00:23:29,760
No.

654
00:23:29,760 --> 00:23:31,440
I wasn't expecting much to begin with.

655
00:23:31,440 --> 00:23:32,160
But it's worth a try.

656
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:33,560
You have to try things
at least once in life.

657
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,640
Honestly, this looks so appetizing.

658
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:37,440
I want to sneak a bite right now.

659
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:37,920
But I guess...

660
00:23:37,920 --> 00:23:39,120
Go ahead and sneak a bite.

661
00:23:39,680 --> 00:23:40,560
Later.

662
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:43,960
Here, chopsticks.

663
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:45,240
They're brand-new.

664
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:48,360
I don't think it's cooked.

665
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:49,120
Want to try some?

666
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:50,000
Later.

667
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:50,640
It's definitely not cooked.

668
00:23:50,640 --> 00:23:51,120
Right?

669
00:23:51,120 --> 00:23:51,600
Don't eat it.

670
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:52,400
It's not cooked.

671
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:54,160
But it's already burnt.

672
00:23:54,440 --> 00:23:55,600
It's already burnt.

673
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:01,640
No, what I mean is

674
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:02,880
we actually like it burnt.

675
00:24:04,210 --> 00:24:06,120
(Mm-hmm, we really do.)
We really do.

676
00:24:06,440 --> 00:24:07,880
It looks like a piece of charcoal.

677
00:24:08,360 --> 00:24:09,360
It looks so appetizing.

678
00:24:12,680 --> 00:24:13,840
Is it okay?

679
00:24:14,560 --> 00:24:15,920
Why does it look like

680
00:24:16,920 --> 00:24:17,800
it's completely burnt?

681
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:18,520
It looks a little...

682
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:19,720
A little...

683
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:20,800
I don't think we can eat this.

684
00:24:20,820 --> 00:24:21,480
(The wok's completely blackened)

685
00:24:21,480 --> 00:24:22,640
There's oil in here.

686
00:24:23,120 --> 00:24:24,280
It's okay. Don't rush.

687
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:26,120
Just scoop out the black liquid.

688
00:24:26,120 --> 00:24:27,200
Then rinse it out one more time.

689
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:28,280
Let me pour it out.

690
00:24:28,280 --> 00:24:28,920
Give me the gloves.

691
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:31,800
A little farther this way.

692
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:32,680
He's trying to get past.

693
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:33,660
(Being considerate)

694
00:24:34,660 --> 00:24:36,040
(Glances)

695
00:24:36,040 --> 00:24:36,600
I'll scrub it for you.

696
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:37,080
Then I'll bring it back.

697
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:38,320
Otherwise, it'll still be black.

698
00:24:38,600 --> 00:24:39,200
Okay.

699
00:24:39,200 --> 00:24:39,960
I'll scrub it and bring it back.

700
00:24:39,960 --> 00:24:40,560
Okay.

701
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:41,800
Thank you.

702
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:43,560
Alright.

703
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:47,240
Here's what we'll do.

704
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:49,960
(Changing the cooking method)
Let's put the meat in first.

705
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:51,320
Why don't we put the meat
and vegetables in together?

706
00:24:51,320 --> 00:24:53,640
I think we should
just stew them all together.

707
00:24:53,640 --> 00:24:55,200
Then add some soybean paste.

708
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:56,120
Add some seasonings.

709
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:56,840
And then, look...

710
00:24:57,040 --> 00:24:58,560
We'll add water.

711
00:25:01,940 --> 00:25:05,220
(Everything goes into one pot)

712
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:06,680
Let's try some of this "dark cuisine".

713
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:09,000
Doesn't it look like a witch...

714
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:09,620
(Adding sauce)

715
00:25:09,620 --> 00:25:10,320
Making some kind of...

716
00:25:10,520 --> 00:25:11,000
"Witch's brew".

717
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:12,400
Yeah, it's "dark cuisine".

718
00:25:14,760 --> 00:25:17,440
I mean, I hate wasting food.

719
00:25:17,440 --> 00:25:18,400
I feel like this entire pot.

720
00:25:18,960 --> 00:25:20,520
I've wasted all these ingredients.

721
00:25:20,520 --> 00:25:21,000
No, you haven't.

722
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:22,160
We're not leaving
until we've finished eating it.

723
00:25:22,680 --> 00:25:23,600
It won't come to that.

724
00:25:24,160 --> 00:25:26,000
We don't have to stuff ourselves

725
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:27,400
just to avoid wasting food.

726
00:25:31,400 --> 00:25:32,240
You're making chicken wings.

727
00:25:34,380 --> 00:25:36,260
(Cui Yihang's second dish:
Garlic butter chicken wings)

728
00:25:38,560 --> 00:25:39,000
I have to say,

729
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:39,800
Cui Yihang's chicken wings

730
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:40,880
look pretty appetizing.

731
00:25:40,880 --> 00:25:41,620
(Praises him)

732
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:44,160
They've got a nice golden-brown color.

733
00:25:51,040 --> 00:25:52,880
You're making one more dish, right?

734
00:25:52,880 --> 00:25:54,560
(Cui Yihang's third dish: Crucian carp soup)
It's crucian carp soup.

735
00:25:54,580 --> 00:25:56,420
(Adding tofu and corn)

736
00:25:56,480 --> 00:25:57,760
Just let it simmer?

737
00:25:57,760 --> 00:25:59,400
Yeah, we can leave it simmering.

738
00:26:00,960 --> 00:26:01,760
That should do it.

739
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:02,620
I think so.

740
00:26:06,570 --> 00:26:08,490
(The crucian carp soup is ready)

741
00:26:08,510 --> 00:26:08,910
What...

742
00:26:09,050 --> 00:26:10,230
(What happened here?)

743
00:26:10,230 --> 00:26:11,150
This looks fine.

744
00:26:12,470 --> 00:26:13,270
It's dried out.

745
00:26:14,110 --> 00:26:14,910
Water.

746
00:26:16,830 --> 00:26:18,070
I think this is how iron-pot stew

747
00:26:18,070 --> 00:26:19,110
is supposed to look.

748
00:26:19,270 --> 00:26:20,390
Iron-pot stew should have a little

749
00:26:20,390 --> 00:26:20,710
more...

750
00:26:20,710 --> 00:26:21,270
Water.

751
00:26:21,270 --> 00:26:22,230
Right, some water should do it.

752
00:26:22,330 --> 00:26:23,230
I let it reduce too much.

753
00:26:24,230 --> 00:26:26,470
I forgot to keep an eye on it.

754
00:26:26,750 --> 00:26:28,070
The potatoes have turned to mush.

755
00:26:28,270 --> 00:26:29,750
The potatoes have turned
to mashed potatoes.

756
00:26:29,750 --> 00:26:31,690
(Iron-pot stew with mashed potatoes)

757
00:26:31,910 --> 00:26:32,870
Now I am curious

758
00:26:32,870 --> 00:26:34,870
how it tastes.

759
00:26:35,670 --> 00:26:36,990
Should this not go on the main table?

760
00:26:36,990 --> 00:26:38,470
I want to see how bad it turned out.

761
00:26:39,100 --> 00:26:39,390
Put...

762
00:26:39,390 --> 00:26:40,870
It doesn't look very appetizing.

763
00:26:40,870 --> 00:26:41,990
Let's not put it in the center.

764
00:26:41,990 --> 00:26:42,790
It ruins the appetite.

765
00:26:42,820 --> 00:26:43,830
(Moving it aside)
No, it won't.

766
00:26:43,830 --> 00:26:45,190
Put it here first.

767
00:26:45,190 --> 00:26:45,870
All right.

768
00:26:45,870 --> 00:26:46,990
Wipe this off.

769
00:26:48,910 --> 00:26:50,190
I will try a green bean first.

770
00:26:50,430 --> 00:26:51,230
It is a little hot.

771
00:26:53,870 --> 00:26:54,870
Is this a green bean?

772
00:26:58,350 --> 00:26:59,110
Is it good?

773
00:27:00,450 --> 00:27:02,290
(Tasting carefully)

774
00:27:05,390 --> 00:27:06,230
A little bitter.

775
00:27:07,070 --> 00:27:08,590
Is it burnt,

776
00:27:08,590 --> 00:27:09,590
or is it the seasoning?

777
00:27:09,590 --> 00:27:10,590
I cannot quite describe it.

778
00:27:11,750 --> 00:27:12,750
It is a little bitter.

779
00:27:13,070 --> 00:27:13,710
It is not great,

780
00:27:13,710 --> 00:27:14,790
but it is not bad either.

781
00:27:14,790 --> 00:27:16,030
I can't quite put
my finger on the taste.

782
00:27:18,870 --> 00:27:20,990
Just turning on the stove

783
00:27:20,990 --> 00:27:22,430
puts you ahead of 99.99% of people.

784
00:27:22,430 --> 00:27:24,390
(Offering encouragement)

785
00:27:24,390 --> 00:27:25,830
I will prepare the crawfish first.

786
00:27:26,290 --> 00:27:28,370
(Sun Bohan's second dish: Crawfish)
Let me see.

787
00:27:30,730 --> 00:27:32,530
(Crawfish goes into the pot)

788
00:27:34,750 --> 00:27:35,710
Is it moving?

789
00:27:37,510 --> 00:27:38,910
It should not be...

790
00:27:39,230 --> 00:27:40,150
Look, it is moving.

791
00:27:40,230 --> 00:27:41,430
Didn't they already remove its head?

792
00:27:41,430 --> 00:27:42,470
Why is it still moving?

793
00:27:42,710 --> 00:27:43,630
Is this...

794
00:27:44,270 --> 00:27:45,190
cooked?

795
00:27:46,110 --> 00:27:47,390
Rinse the crawfish thoroughly.

796
00:27:47,910 --> 00:27:49,630
(Checking the instructions again)
Deep-fry until the shells turn red.

797
00:27:49,630 --> 00:27:51,070
But they are already red.

798
00:27:51,070 --> 00:27:52,030
Yes.

799
00:27:52,030 --> 00:27:53,710
Let's start over.

800
00:27:55,070 --> 00:27:55,870
Garlic flavor.

801
00:27:56,370 --> 00:27:59,930
(Adding the seasoning packet)

802
00:28:01,790 --> 00:28:03,150
Now add the crawfish.

803
00:28:04,850 --> 00:28:08,490
(Crawfish goes into the pot)

804
00:28:08,630 --> 00:28:09,910
This looks pretty good.

805
00:28:10,510 --> 00:28:12,150
(The color is rich and vibrant)
That means I still have room to improve.

806
00:28:12,150 --> 00:28:12,950
Yes.

807
00:28:12,950 --> 00:28:14,030
Just add the beer directly.

808
00:28:14,030 --> 00:28:15,650
(Pouring in the beer)

809
00:28:16,790 --> 00:28:17,550
Has the liquid evaporated?

810
00:28:17,550 --> 00:28:19,150
I think it should be ready, right?

811
00:28:20,270 --> 00:28:21,070
I will pour it in here.

812
00:28:21,070 --> 00:28:21,590
All right.

813
00:28:28,430 --> 00:28:30,790
Your dishes are always
so carefully presented.

814
00:28:30,790 --> 00:28:33,070
Mine are either in a basin or a bowl.

815
00:28:34,070 --> 00:28:35,110
From now on, when I get home,

816
00:28:35,110 --> 00:28:36,350
I must improve my cooking skills.

817
00:28:37,110 --> 00:28:37,750
Sit down.

818
00:28:42,050 --> 00:28:43,570
(Picks up food)

819
00:28:45,510 --> 00:28:46,670
I am left-handed.

820
00:28:47,070 --> 00:28:48,190
That is impressive.

821
00:28:48,190 --> 00:28:49,350
You use chopsticks with your left hand.

822
00:28:53,010 --> 00:28:54,530
(Laughing)

823
00:29:04,030 --> 00:29:05,230
This is good.

824
00:29:08,550 --> 00:29:11,070
Actually, I think the ribs are better.

825
00:29:11,070 --> 00:29:13,930
(Choosing carefully)

826
00:29:15,690 --> 00:29:17,850
(Examining it closely)

827
00:29:17,950 --> 00:29:19,310
Would you be okay

828
00:29:19,310 --> 00:29:20,310
with this smaller piece?

829
00:29:20,310 --> 00:29:21,110
All right.

830
00:29:22,890 --> 00:29:24,290
(Tasting)

831
00:29:25,370 --> 00:29:26,570
(Watching closely)

832
00:29:28,150 --> 00:29:28,990
It is delicious.

833
00:29:29,830 --> 00:29:30,510
Really.

834
00:29:32,870 --> 00:29:33,550
It is fine.

835
00:29:33,550 --> 00:29:35,670
I am aware
of my own cooking abilities.

836
00:29:35,670 --> 00:29:36,350
Besides, I never

837
00:29:36,350 --> 00:29:37,790
used to eat ribs.

838
00:29:38,470 --> 00:29:39,070
Why not?

839
00:29:39,390 --> 00:29:40,630
Because I had never had good ribs.

840
00:29:42,010 --> 00:29:43,970
(Happy)

841
00:29:46,990 --> 00:29:48,550
Which dish do you think is the best?

842
00:29:50,750 --> 00:29:51,590
(Choosing the coconut curry chicken)
This one.

843
00:29:51,590 --> 00:29:52,590
I like this one too.

844
00:29:53,050 --> 00:29:53,560
Eat up.

845
00:30:00,630 --> 00:30:01,350
Where are the potatoes?

846
00:30:01,670 --> 00:30:03,030
They have all turned
into mashed potatoes.

847
00:30:08,130 --> 00:30:09,330
(Picks up food)

848
00:30:12,410 --> 00:30:14,370
(Takes a small bite)

849
00:30:18,270 --> 00:30:18,950
It's good.

850
00:30:19,730 --> 00:30:21,650
(Happy)

851
00:30:22,150 --> 00:30:22,990
Try the dish

852
00:30:22,990 --> 00:30:23,830
Cui Yihang made first.

853
00:30:24,450 --> 00:30:27,010
(Feeding him a bite)

854
00:30:27,150 --> 00:30:27,750
It is delicious.

855
00:30:29,190 --> 00:30:30,070
The curry flavor is rich.

856
00:30:30,670 --> 00:30:32,710
It rivals the Thai restaurant
we went to,

857
00:30:33,390 --> 00:30:34,030
right?

858
00:30:38,210 --> 00:30:39,490
(Smiles)

859
00:30:39,510 --> 00:30:41,070
It is even better
than the Thai restaurant.

860
00:30:41,070 --> 00:30:41,770
(Praises)

861
00:30:41,950 --> 00:30:42,990
Really.

862
00:30:42,990 --> 00:30:43,870
Look at you smiling.

863
00:30:45,750 --> 00:30:46,870
It is a little healthier too.

864
00:30:48,110 --> 00:30:49,110
The color of the fish soup

865
00:30:49,110 --> 00:30:50,070
alone makes it look authentic.

866
00:30:50,910 --> 00:30:51,430
Very authentic.

867
00:30:53,590 --> 00:30:54,390
Give it a try.

868
00:30:55,210 --> 00:30:57,650
(Tasting)

869
00:30:59,310 --> 00:31:00,350
It is really good.

870
00:31:00,590 --> 00:31:00,990
Really.

871
00:31:00,990 --> 00:31:01,870
It tastes wonderful.

872
00:31:04,470 --> 00:31:06,550
Cui Yihang has the makings of a great chef.

873
00:31:13,270 --> 00:31:15,110
Which dish do you think

874
00:31:15,110 --> 00:31:16,230
tastes the best today?

875
00:31:16,990 --> 00:31:17,910
I like this one.

876
00:31:17,910 --> 00:31:18,650
(Wu Siying chooses
the coconut curry chicken)

877
00:31:21,510 --> 00:31:22,470
Do you want some?

878
00:31:22,750 --> 00:31:23,630
Go ahead.

879
00:31:24,950 --> 00:31:25,870
Here, it is dripping.

880
00:31:26,610 --> 00:31:27,490
(Feeding him a bite)

881
00:31:32,350 --> 00:31:34,270
I like it. My favorite
is the iron-pot stew.

882
00:31:34,270 --> 00:31:34,870
No.

883
00:31:34,870 --> 00:31:36,750
(Wu Xingying chooses the iron-pot stew)
Will this affect the rating?

884
00:31:37,030 --> 00:31:37,750
That's fair.

885
00:31:37,750 --> 00:31:38,950
Si gets me.

886
00:31:38,950 --> 00:31:39,910
Is that what I meant?

887
00:31:41,550 --> 00:31:42,310
That is what she means.

888
00:31:43,370 --> 00:31:44,170
(Cannot hold back laughter)

889
00:31:44,270 --> 00:31:45,310
This dish is already impressive.

890
00:31:45,310 --> 00:31:47,350
It is usually only
served in restaurants.

891
00:31:47,790 --> 00:31:48,750
Just getting it to the table

892
00:31:48,750 --> 00:31:49,750
is an achievement.

893
00:31:50,550 --> 00:31:53,750
Cui Yihang is very encouraging.

894
00:31:54,270 --> 00:31:54,750
Some people

895
00:31:54,750 --> 00:31:56,950
deliberately make a dish like this.

896
00:31:56,950 --> 00:31:58,150
Mashed potatoes with ribs.

897
00:31:58,160 --> 00:31:58,600
Yes.

898
00:31:59,470 --> 00:31:59,870
Really.

899
00:31:59,870 --> 00:32:00,510
Yes.

900
00:32:00,770 --> 00:32:01,650
(Cannot hold back laughter)

901
00:32:02,270 --> 00:32:03,070
Really.

902
00:32:04,030 --> 00:32:05,470
It really is quite unique.

903
00:32:05,470 --> 00:32:07,030
You do not have to make me feel better.

904
00:32:07,030 --> 00:32:07,830
But honestly,

905
00:32:08,190 --> 00:32:09,270
I am not that disappointed, either.

906
00:32:09,270 --> 00:32:10,470
It is my first time making this.

907
00:32:10,470 --> 00:32:11,510
This is not encouragement.

908
00:32:12,510 --> 00:32:13,390
Besides, all three of us

909
00:32:13,390 --> 00:32:14,790
prefer our food slightly charred.

910
00:32:17,990 --> 00:32:19,030
I am already quite happy

911
00:32:19,030 --> 00:32:20,150
that it does not taste terrible.

912
00:32:20,590 --> 00:32:22,190
All three of you
have been so supportive.

913
00:32:22,190 --> 00:32:23,070
I am really happy.

914
00:32:23,430 --> 00:32:24,350
We are not just being nice.

915
00:32:24,550 --> 00:32:25,630
You are overthinking it.

916
00:32:26,030 --> 00:32:27,470
You won't even let us be honest.

917
00:32:28,790 --> 00:32:29,870
Did you all enjoy yourselves today?

918
00:32:30,310 --> 00:32:31,590
I enjoyed it immensely.

919
00:32:32,430 --> 00:32:34,230
On a scale of one to ten,
what would you give it?

920
00:32:34,750 --> 00:32:35,510
Ten.

921
00:32:35,510 --> 00:32:36,450
(Giving it a 10)
Ten.

922
00:32:36,470 --> 00:32:36,870
And you?

923
00:32:36,870 --> 00:32:37,750
Ten.

924
00:32:37,750 --> 00:32:38,430
It was a little tiring,

925
00:32:38,430 --> 00:32:39,230
but it was a lot of fun.

926
00:32:39,830 --> 00:32:40,150
Yes.

927
00:32:40,150 --> 00:32:40,950
Although we were sweating

928
00:32:40,950 --> 00:32:41,870
the whole time,

929
00:32:41,870 --> 00:32:42,790
it was a unique experience.

930
00:32:43,910 --> 00:32:46,470
I have taken the first step, too.

931
00:32:46,470 --> 00:32:47,990
There is still

932
00:32:47,990 --> 00:32:49,270
plenty of room for improvement,

933
00:32:49,270 --> 00:32:50,590
but it was a good experience.

934
00:32:50,590 --> 00:32:51,710
This corn from the iron-pot stew

935
00:32:51,710 --> 00:32:52,550
is especially delicious.

936
00:32:52,950 --> 00:32:54,470
I am easily pleased.

937
00:32:55,550 --> 00:32:56,550
I was telling Xing that the last

938
00:32:56,550 --> 00:32:58,190
time we ate together
was on confession night.

939
00:32:59,110 --> 00:32:59,710
Yes.

940
00:32:59,870 --> 00:33:01,590
It has already been a month.

941
00:33:01,950 --> 00:33:02,670
Is it fast?

942
00:33:02,670 --> 00:33:03,670
It was right here,

943
00:33:04,190 --> 00:33:05,110
in the same spot.

944
00:33:05,710 --> 00:33:06,510
It was right here.

945
00:33:06,670 --> 00:33:07,110
Right?

946
00:33:07,110 --> 00:33:08,230
Right here, yes.

947
00:33:08,710 --> 00:33:09,790
That's pretty amazing.

948
00:33:10,350 --> 00:33:11,110
Ever since

949
00:33:11,470 --> 00:33:12,310
I met you,

950
00:33:12,310 --> 00:33:13,550
I have done so many things

951
00:33:13,550 --> 00:33:14,870
I've never done before.

952
00:33:15,050 --> 00:33:15,870
(Laughing)

953
00:33:15,870 --> 00:33:17,310
I said that two people

954
00:33:17,870 --> 00:33:19,190
should try new

955
00:33:19,190 --> 00:33:20,990
things together.

956
00:33:21,030 --> 00:33:22,430
(Two people should try new things together)
It is interesting.

957
00:33:22,470 --> 00:33:23,310
Was cooking crawfish

958
00:33:23,310 --> 00:33:24,510
the first time you did

959
00:33:24,510 --> 00:33:25,990
after arriving

960
00:33:26,150 --> 00:33:26,830
at the Signal House?

961
00:33:27,390 --> 00:33:28,070
It was my first time.

962
00:33:29,990 --> 00:33:31,590
How have you two been this past month?

963
00:33:32,430 --> 00:33:33,590
I think things have been going well.

964
00:33:34,470 --> 00:33:36,710
I feel that you are the same

965
00:33:36,710 --> 00:33:38,310
as you were

966
00:33:38,310 --> 00:33:39,310
on confession night.

967
00:33:41,190 --> 00:33:42,510
So I haven't made any progress?

968
00:33:42,870 --> 00:33:43,430
No.

969
00:33:43,430 --> 00:33:43,750
Really?

970
00:33:43,750 --> 00:33:45,630
The more time people spend together,

971
00:33:47,070 --> 00:33:49,670
the more comfortable
they become with each other.

972
00:33:50,670 --> 00:33:52,590
But getting too comfortable

973
00:33:52,590 --> 00:33:53,910
is not always a good thing.

974
00:33:53,910 --> 00:33:54,710
It might not always feel...

975
00:33:55,190 --> 00:33:55,510
Yes.

976
00:33:55,510 --> 00:33:56,430
As exciting...

977
00:33:56,670 --> 00:33:58,390
As it did at first.

978
00:33:58,390 --> 00:33:59,030
But you are still

979
00:33:59,030 --> 00:34:00,590
the same as you were
on confession night.

980
00:34:01,630 --> 00:34:03,030
I think things are even better now

981
00:34:03,030 --> 00:34:03,910
than they were that night.

982
00:34:04,790 --> 00:34:05,590
What is better?

983
00:34:05,590 --> 00:34:06,390
Tell me.

984
00:34:09,150 --> 00:34:10,070
Everything is wonderful.

985
00:34:10,550 --> 00:34:12,230
Life here is better

986
00:34:12,230 --> 00:34:13,910
than all the stars in the sky.

987
00:34:14,510 --> 00:34:16,310
Better than all the stars in the sky.

988
00:34:16,310 --> 00:34:19,930
(Better than all the stars in the sky)

989
00:34:21,430 --> 00:34:22,230
Happy life.

990
00:34:23,390 --> 00:34:24,550
You two are so sweet.

991
00:34:26,130 --> 00:34:27,770
(Smiles)

992
00:34:27,790 --> 00:34:29,230
How have you two been this past month?

993
00:34:29,470 --> 00:34:30,710
Pretty good.

994
00:34:32,510 --> 00:34:33,350
What do you think?

995
00:34:34,070 --> 00:34:35,030
She has changed so much.

996
00:34:35,030 --> 00:34:35,870
No.

997
00:34:36,990 --> 00:34:38,590
Has she changed for the better, then?

998
00:34:38,590 --> 00:34:39,790
Of course she has.

999
00:34:39,790 --> 00:34:41,110
She has become even more adorable.

1000
00:34:42,470 --> 00:34:43,630
That was a very sincere answer.

1001
00:34:47,110 --> 00:34:48,070
Do you two

1002
00:34:48,070 --> 00:34:49,670
video call each other often?

1003
00:34:49,670 --> 00:34:50,270
We...

1004
00:34:50,870 --> 00:34:52,110
We do when we cannot meet in person.

1005
00:34:53,430 --> 00:34:55,910
Who usually initiates the calls?

1006
00:34:55,910 --> 00:34:56,830
It is definitely Cui Yihang.

1007
00:34:56,830 --> 00:34:57,630
(Of course it is me)
Is it not obvious?

1008
00:34:57,630 --> 00:34:58,710
Cui Yihang is the one who initiates.

1009
00:34:59,790 --> 00:35:00,750
Most of the time.

1010
00:35:00,750 --> 00:35:01,630
Not just most of the time.

1011
00:35:01,630 --> 00:35:02,710
It seems like it is always him.

1012
00:35:03,710 --> 00:35:04,590
Pretty much.

1013
00:35:05,430 --> 00:35:06,950
But I think the four of us

1014
00:35:07,310 --> 00:35:09,230
have grown a lot closer

1015
00:35:09,230 --> 00:35:10,390
over the past month.

1016
00:35:12,310 --> 00:35:13,350
We have become much closer.

1017
00:35:15,680 --> 00:35:17,230
It feels like we are more of a family now.

1018
00:35:20,830 --> 00:35:22,150
You both have older sisters,

1019
00:35:22,150 --> 00:35:22,670
right?

1020
00:35:23,070 --> 00:35:24,630
Yes, I have an older sister.

1021
00:35:25,550 --> 00:35:26,550
Cui Yihang has two.

1022
00:35:26,550 --> 00:35:27,270
Yes, I have two.

1023
00:35:28,070 --> 00:35:28,750
Yes.

1024
00:35:28,750 --> 00:35:30,030
Even though I have an older sister,

1025
00:35:30,030 --> 00:35:32,470
I grew up quite differently from you.

1026
00:35:33,110 --> 00:35:34,510
That is because my sister

1027
00:35:34,510 --> 00:35:35,510
moved to Harbin

1028
00:35:35,510 --> 00:35:36,230
when I was about three

1029
00:35:36,230 --> 00:35:37,190
or four years old.

1030
00:35:38,190 --> 00:35:39,030
Even though

1031
00:35:39,030 --> 00:35:40,470
I have an older sister,
we grew up apart,

1032
00:35:40,470 --> 00:35:41,670
so I grew up like an only child.

1033
00:35:41,670 --> 00:35:42,870
(I barely spent time
with my sister growing up)

1034
00:35:42,870 --> 00:35:44,510
My sister is also
12 years older than me.

1035
00:35:44,830 --> 00:35:46,390
Do you remember much

1036
00:35:46,390 --> 00:35:47,670
about her when you were little?

1037
00:35:48,350 --> 00:35:49,230
I do,

1038
00:35:49,230 --> 00:35:51,470
but not very much.

1039
00:35:51,590 --> 00:35:52,630
Did you look forward to her

1040
00:35:52,630 --> 00:35:53,910
coming home every Chinese New Year?

1041
00:35:53,910 --> 00:35:55,270
Of course.

1042
00:35:56,430 --> 00:35:57,470
The more, the merrier.

1043
00:35:58,870 --> 00:35:59,750
What about you, Cui Yihang?

1044
00:36:00,310 --> 00:36:01,870
You have two older sisters.

1045
00:36:01,870 --> 00:36:03,070
How many years older are they?

1046
00:36:03,430 --> 00:36:05,270
One is three years older,
and the other is seven.

1047
00:36:05,270 --> 00:36:06,470
So, you grew up together?

1048
00:36:06,950 --> 00:36:07,790
More or less.

1049
00:36:07,810 --> 00:36:09,350
(He grew up with his sisters)
We grew up together.

1050
00:36:09,360 --> 00:36:10,030
That is nice.

1051
00:36:10,150 --> 00:36:11,070
Have you two ever

1052
00:36:11,070 --> 00:36:12,030
had a serious argument?

1053
00:36:12,030 --> 00:36:12,830
Physical fights.

1054
00:36:15,190 --> 00:36:15,950
You two fought, too?

1055
00:36:16,910 --> 00:36:17,910
How did you fight?

1056
00:36:18,230 --> 00:36:20,070
I told him before that we went

1057
00:36:20,070 --> 00:36:21,870
all out when we fought.

1058
00:36:21,990 --> 00:36:23,070
Really? You two...

1059
00:36:23,270 --> 00:36:24,870
We really went all out
when we fought as kids.

1060
00:36:25,030 --> 00:36:26,510
Were your fights really that serious?

1061
00:36:26,950 --> 00:36:27,990
It was over very trivial things.

1062
00:36:28,550 --> 00:36:29,430
For example,

1063
00:36:29,430 --> 00:36:30,750
I might have wanted pink slippers,

1064
00:36:30,750 --> 00:36:31,910
and she would want

1065
00:36:31,910 --> 00:36:33,470
the same pair.

1066
00:36:33,870 --> 00:36:34,590
It'd be something trivial.

1067
00:36:36,350 --> 00:36:37,870
Have you ever argued with your sister?

1068
00:36:38,230 --> 00:36:40,030
No, not once in my life.

1069
00:36:40,030 --> 00:36:41,190
Maybe it's because she lived

1070
00:36:41,190 --> 00:36:42,350
so far away when I was growing up.

1071
00:36:43,270 --> 00:36:45,550
She was almost like

1072
00:36:45,550 --> 00:36:46,910
a second mom to me.

1073
00:36:47,750 --> 00:36:49,390
We only saw each other

1074
00:36:49,390 --> 00:36:50,670
once a year, during Chinese New Year.

1075
00:36:50,670 --> 00:36:52,110
She was almost like
an elder to you, right?

1076
00:36:52,110 --> 00:36:52,790
Yes.

1077
00:36:53,870 --> 00:36:54,510
His sister

1078
00:36:54,510 --> 00:36:56,230
was born in the same zodiac year as us.

1079
00:36:56,950 --> 00:36:58,150
Exactly one zodiac cycle older.

1080
00:36:58,470 --> 00:36:59,710
What a coincidence.

1081
00:37:00,350 --> 00:37:02,790
I am quite curious
about what your childhoods were like.

1082
00:37:02,790 --> 00:37:03,570
(Curious)

1083
00:37:04,110 --> 00:37:05,630
Let's see if they can tell us apart.

1084
00:37:06,390 --> 00:37:07,030
Sure.

1085
00:37:07,830 --> 00:37:08,430
Here.

1086
00:37:09,430 --> 00:37:10,430
Let me guess.

1087
00:37:12,030 --> 00:37:13,030
This is obviously you.

1088
00:37:13,030 --> 00:37:15,010
(Bohan guesses: Xing left, Si right)
That big smile has to be Si.

1089
00:37:15,030 --> 00:37:15,870
Cui Yihang, look.

1090
00:37:16,830 --> 00:37:18,230
Try telling us apart.

1091
00:37:19,910 --> 00:37:21,730
(Cui Yihang guesses: Xing left, Si right)
That's her.

1092
00:37:21,750 --> 00:37:23,630
I also think the one
with the big smile is Si.

1093
00:37:23,790 --> 00:37:24,830
Tell us the answer.

1094
00:37:25,030 --> 00:37:26,630
The one smiling is Xing.

1095
00:37:26,660 --> 00:37:27,910
(Both got it wrong)
You both got it wrong.

1096
00:37:27,910 --> 00:37:29,710
How have your personalities changed
over the years?

1097
00:37:29,710 --> 00:37:30,590
You can't judge by personality.

1098
00:37:30,590 --> 00:37:32,270
How did things

1099
00:37:32,270 --> 00:37:33,790
end up completely reversed?

1100
00:37:35,550 --> 00:37:36,510
You were so calm as a kid.

1101
00:37:36,990 --> 00:37:38,870
You were judging by our expressions?

1102
00:37:38,870 --> 00:37:39,510
What about you?

1103
00:37:39,510 --> 00:37:41,830
I was going by your build.

1104
00:37:41,830 --> 00:37:42,470
Didn't you

1105
00:37:42,470 --> 00:37:43,830
grow faster when you were little?

1106
00:37:44,990 --> 00:37:46,270
Guess not.

1107
00:37:49,290 --> 00:37:52,450
(Second photo)

1108
00:37:52,990 --> 00:37:54,030
(Bohan guesses: Si left, Xing right)
The one on the left is Si.

1109
00:37:54,030 --> 00:37:54,870
You're on the right.

1110
00:37:56,990 --> 00:37:57,470
This is you.

1111
00:37:57,470 --> 00:37:58,370
(Cui Yihang guesses: Xing left, Si right)
That's Xing.

1112
00:37:58,370 --> 00:37:59,310
What's the answer?

1113
00:37:59,310 --> 00:38:00,310
Cui Yihang got it right.

1114
00:38:00,310 --> 00:38:00,790
Yep.

1115
00:38:01,310 --> 00:38:02,150
I'm on the left.

1116
00:38:02,990 --> 00:38:04,110
(Third photo)
I think that's you.

1117
00:38:04,110 --> 00:38:04,910
That's Si.

1118
00:38:05,030 --> 00:38:06,310
(Bohan guesses: Si left, Xing right)
Si's on the left and...

1119
00:38:06,310 --> 00:38:07,110
Si's on the left. I'm on the right.

1120
00:38:07,110 --> 00:38:07,350
Go ahead.

1121
00:38:07,950 --> 00:38:09,830
I think the one on the right is...

1122
00:38:09,830 --> 00:38:10,910
(Cui Yihang guesses: Si right, Xing left)
The opposite of his guess.

1123
00:38:11,070 --> 00:38:11,870
Cui Yihang got it right.

1124
00:38:11,870 --> 00:38:12,980
(Cui Yihang gets it right again)
Yep.

1125
00:38:13,070 --> 00:38:13,870
That's me.

1126
00:38:15,750 --> 00:38:17,790
Why were you always
the lively one as a kid?

1127
00:38:18,510 --> 00:38:19,910
They look pretty different too.

1128
00:38:19,910 --> 00:38:21,350
Yeah. You can't go
by who's more lively.

1129
00:38:21,350 --> 00:38:22,830
It's about our looks.

1130
00:38:22,830 --> 00:38:24,390
How can you tell by your looks?

1131
00:38:26,190 --> 00:38:27,710
Those eyes and eyebrows
are definitely Si's.

1132
00:38:29,190 --> 00:38:30,990
(Fourth photo)
Cui Yihang, you guess first.

1133
00:38:31,110 --> 00:38:32,190
I'll guess the opposite.

1134
00:38:32,710 --> 00:38:33,590
This was during Chinese New Year.

1135
00:38:33,590 --> 00:38:34,310
He knows this one.

1136
00:38:34,310 --> 00:38:34,830
