Three, two, one!

1412
00:46:24,270 --> 00:46:24,550
Go!

1413
00:46:31,310 --> 00:46:37,110
(Cao Yiheng's POV)
We're going off-roading today.

1414
00:46:37,110 --> 00:46:38,070
A UTV.

1415
00:46:38,890 --> 00:46:40,610
(Excited)

1416
00:46:40,630 --> 00:46:42,390
I've wanted to try this forever.

1417
00:46:42,390 --> 00:46:43,670
Now you finally get to.

1418
00:46:43,670 --> 00:46:45,230
It's finally happening.

1419
00:46:49,070 --> 00:46:50,960
Let's get out.

1420
00:46:55,230 --> 00:46:56,230
So many vehicles!

1421
00:46:56,230 --> 00:46:57,610
(An off-road park in Beijing)

1422
00:47:02,150 --> 00:47:03,390
Hi!

1423
00:47:03,390 --> 00:47:04,480
(Off-road instructor)
Hi.

1424
00:47:04,630 --> 00:47:05,230
You first, sir?

1425
00:47:05,230 --> 00:47:05,750
Or you, miss?

1426
00:47:05,750 --> 00:47:06,470
You go first.

1427
00:47:06,470 --> 00:47:07,430
Okay, I'll go first.

1428
00:47:08,310 --> 00:47:09,270
Come on, hop in.

1429
00:47:10,870 --> 00:47:12,710
I can't drive this thing.

1430
00:47:13,150 --> 00:47:13,670
I'll drive.

1431
00:47:13,670 --> 00:47:14,830
(Cao Yiheng takes the wheel)

1432
00:47:14,830 --> 00:47:15,950
How do I buckle this?

1433
00:47:16,310 --> 00:47:17,150
Let me see.

1434
00:47:19,510 --> 00:47:19,990
One sec.

1435
00:47:19,990 --> 00:47:21,030
Let me buckle you in.

1436
00:47:21,710 --> 00:47:22,750
Just slip it over your shoulders.

1437
00:47:22,750 --> 00:47:23,430
Like this?

1438
00:47:23,430 --> 00:47:24,230
Yep.

1439
00:47:24,230 --> 00:47:25,110
Bring that other strap over.

1440
00:47:25,110 --> 00:47:26,750
You've even got a walkie-talkie.

1441
00:47:26,750 --> 00:47:27,750
A walkie-talkie too?

1442
00:47:27,750 --> 00:47:28,470
If there's an emergency,

1443
00:47:28,470 --> 00:47:29,310
use the walkie-talkie

1444
00:47:29,310 --> 00:47:30,430
to call the instructor up ahead.

1445
00:47:30,430 --> 00:47:31,510
You've got a loud voice.

1446
00:47:31,510 --> 00:47:33,190
You could just yell to the instructor.

1447
00:47:33,190 --> 00:47:34,710
Help!

1448
00:47:35,170 --> 00:47:36,410
(Laughs)

1449
00:47:37,470 --> 00:47:38,870
Just follow the vehicle ahead.

1450
00:47:38,870 --> 00:47:39,390
Got it.

1451
00:47:39,390 --> 00:47:40,150
Let's go!

1452
00:47:41,330 --> 00:47:44,650
(Cui Kaiyi's POV)

1453
00:47:47,410 --> 00:47:50,890
(Cui Kaiyi's POV)

1454
00:47:54,270 --> 00:47:54,870
Let's go!

1455
00:47:54,870 --> 00:47:55,730
(Off we go)

1456
00:47:55,970 --> 00:47:57,050
(Speeds up)

1457
00:47:58,730 --> 00:47:59,650
(Totally immersed)

1458
00:48:00,250 --> 00:48:01,610
(Driving steadily)

1459
00:48:02,050 --> 00:48:03,290
(Entering the off-road trail)

1460
00:48:09,430 --> 00:48:10,590
It's so steep!

1461
00:48:11,150 --> 00:48:12,430
It's all downhill!

1462
00:48:14,230 --> 00:48:16,950
Keep your mouth closed, babe.

1463
00:48:17,610 --> 00:48:18,210
(Closes mouth)

1464
00:48:18,470 --> 00:48:20,650
Your throat will hurt
if you keep it open.

1465
00:48:20,650 --> 00:48:21,830
(Looking out for her)
Okay.

1466
00:48:22,390 --> 00:48:24,430
I feel like I just swallowed
a mouthful of dirt.

1467
00:48:24,430 --> 00:48:25,670
Me too.

1468
00:48:27,910 --> 00:48:29,430
All the dust from the vehicles ahead

1469
00:48:29,430 --> 00:48:30,990
is blowing right into our faces.

1470
00:48:36,050 --> 00:48:37,610
(Glances)

1471
00:48:37,630 --> 00:48:39,150
You're amazing!

1472
00:48:39,150 --> 00:48:40,510
You really know how to steer.

1473
00:48:40,510 --> 00:48:42,070
(Showering him with compliments)
Of course.

1474
00:48:42,490 --> 00:48:44,930
(Leans closer)

1475
00:48:46,730 --> 00:48:48,010
(Glances)

1476
00:48:51,530 --> 00:48:53,330
(Filming)

1477
00:48:54,990 --> 00:48:56,310
Having fun?

1478
00:48:56,310 --> 00:48:57,110
Yeah.

1479
00:48:58,320 --> 00:48:59,580
Watch out for that branch.

1480
00:48:59,580 --> 00:49:00,190
(Warns her)
Okay.

1481
00:49:02,890 --> 00:49:03,370
(Holds on)

1482
00:49:03,390 --> 00:49:06,230
Feels like we're exploring the jungle.

1483
00:49:07,890 --> 00:49:08,570
(45° slope)

1484
00:49:08,590 --> 00:49:09,670
(Here comes the real thrill)
We're going straight down!

1485
00:49:09,690 --> 00:49:11,850
(Super excited)

1486
00:49:13,330 --> 00:49:14,970
(Grabs on with both hands)

1487
00:49:14,970 --> 00:49:17,240
Whoa!

1488
00:49:18,110 --> 00:49:19,430
That was terrifying!

1489
00:49:19,430 --> 00:49:21,550
That was fun!

1490
00:49:21,550 --> 00:49:22,750
This looks so hard to drive.

1491
00:49:22,750 --> 00:49:24,310
You're amazing, babe.

1492
00:49:24,830 --> 00:49:26,350
(Showing off his driving skills)
You're so good.

1493
00:49:27,050 --> 00:49:28,730
(Whoa)

1494
00:49:30,390 --> 00:49:33,670
They should make
a whole compilation of your reactions.

1495
00:49:33,770 --> 00:49:36,330
(Excited version)

1496
00:49:36,370 --> 00:49:37,530
(Calm version)

1497
00:49:37,650 --> 00:49:38,610
(Thrilled version)

1498
00:49:38,690 --> 00:49:39,530
(Exhausted version)

1499
00:49:48,390 --> 00:49:49,750
Here it comes!

1500
00:49:49,750 --> 00:49:50,990
We're here.

1501
00:49:51,490 --> 00:49:52,770
(A series of steep slopes)
Speed up.

1502
00:49:52,810 --> 00:49:54,170
(Accelerating)

1503
00:50:04,070 --> 00:50:05,150
This is so much fun!

1504
00:50:05,150 --> 00:50:06,430
I love this!

1505
00:50:10,270 --> 00:50:11,990
We're bouncing all over!

1506
00:50:11,990 --> 00:50:13,190
There's water!

1507
00:50:13,190 --> 00:50:14,990
Here comes the mud!

1508
00:50:14,990 --> 00:50:16,190
(Mud pit ahead)
I'm gonna charge through.

1509
00:50:16,430 --> 00:50:17,350
Go for it!

1510
00:50:17,900 --> 00:50:18,550
Okay!

1511
00:50:20,330 --> 00:50:21,490
(Picking up speed)

1512
00:50:26,930 --> 00:50:28,490
(Mud splashing everywhere)

1513
00:50:30,010 --> 00:50:31,150
Oh, no!

1514
00:50:31,150 --> 00:50:31,950
We're covered in mud!

1515
00:50:32,550 --> 00:50:33,590
Cao Yiheng!

1516
00:50:37,110 --> 00:50:38,870
It's all your fault!

1517
00:50:39,650 --> 00:50:40,850
(New look unlocked)

1518
00:50:41,270 --> 00:50:42,550
It's fine.
We're only wearing these today.

1519
00:50:42,550 --> 00:50:43,680
We'll change when we get back.

1520
00:50:43,680 --> 00:50:44,300
Okay.

1521
00:50:48,090 --> 00:50:48,850
(Look at my face)

1522
00:50:50,150 --> 00:50:51,710
Is there a lot on my face?

1523
00:50:51,710 --> 00:50:53,670
Not much. What about mine?

1524
00:50:53,670 --> 00:50:54,950
Not much either.

1525
00:50:54,950 --> 00:50:55,970
It's like a coffee facial.

1526
00:50:55,970 --> 00:50:56,490
(Staying positive)

1527
00:51:00,310 --> 00:51:01,470
Are we back?

1528
00:51:01,470 --> 00:51:02,270
(Back at the starting point)
Yep.

1529
00:51:03,390 --> 00:51:04,350
Home sweet home.

1530
00:51:06,450 --> 00:51:07,770
(Checks the mirror)

1531
00:51:07,770 --> 00:51:09,150
Oh my God!

1532
00:51:09,150 --> 00:51:10,830
My face!

1533
00:51:12,430 --> 00:51:14,110
My face!

1534
00:51:14,110 --> 00:51:15,370
My pants!

1535
00:51:15,370 --> 00:51:16,370
(Glances)

1536
00:51:16,710 --> 00:51:17,870
They're tie-dyed now.

1537
00:51:17,870 --> 00:51:19,150
I've got tie-dye pants.

1538
00:51:19,150 --> 00:51:20,710
(Complimenting her)
Yours actually look good.

1539
00:51:20,870 --> 00:51:22,830
Looks like I peed my pants.

1540
00:51:22,830 --> 00:51:24,670
Yours look like tiger stripes.

1541
00:51:29,390 --> 00:51:30,350
Thanks.

1542
00:51:30,350 --> 00:51:30,790
You're welcome.

1543
00:51:31,650 --> 00:51:33,010
(Fixing her hair)

1544
00:51:34,490 --> 00:51:35,500
Does it look okay?

1545
00:51:35,500 --> 00:51:36,350
Yeah.

1546
00:51:36,350 --> 00:51:37,910
Let's change and grab some food.

1547
00:51:37,910 --> 00:51:38,870
I saw this coming.

1548
00:51:38,870 --> 00:51:40,430
I even brought a change of clothes.

1549
00:51:42,710 --> 00:51:43,590
Let's go eat then.

1550
00:51:43,590 --> 00:51:44,470
- Let's change first.
- Let's go.

1551
00:51:44,470 --> 00:51:45,630
These are soaked.

1552
00:51:45,630 --> 00:51:47,430
Your clothes are holding water.

1553
00:51:47,430 --> 00:51:49,670
I'm a walking coffee machine now.

1554
00:51:52,830 --> 00:51:54,470
Time to eat!

1555
00:52:02,700 --> 00:52:03,300
Want some water?

1556
00:52:03,300 --> 00:52:04,370
Yes.

1557
00:52:04,930 --> 00:52:06,930
(Unscrews the cap)

1558
00:52:07,330 --> 00:52:08,810
(Hands it over)
Thanks.

1559
00:52:30,110 --> 00:52:30,630
Mwah!

1560
00:52:34,950 --> 00:52:37,590
Look, he's all the way up the mountain.

1561
00:52:39,510 --> 00:52:41,350
Look at this.

1562
00:52:41,350 --> 00:52:42,310
The village.

1563
00:52:43,510 --> 00:52:44,470
I like it.

1564
00:52:45,150 --> 00:52:46,270
What if we lived here someday?

1565
00:52:46,270 --> 00:52:47,430
That'd actually be nice.

1566
00:52:47,430 --> 00:52:49,310
How would you order milk tea out here?

1567
00:52:49,910 --> 00:52:50,990
Yeah, I couldn't.

1568
00:52:50,990 --> 00:52:52,390
But we could make our own.

1569
00:52:53,630 --> 00:52:55,070
Make our own milk tea?

1570
00:52:57,950 --> 00:52:58,790
Not bad.

1571
00:52:58,790 --> 00:52:59,390
See?

1572
00:52:59,670 --> 00:53:00,550
Right?

1573
00:53:02,510 --> 00:53:03,190
I feel like

1574
00:53:03,190 --> 00:53:05,310
this place has a Thailand vibe.

1575
00:53:05,310 --> 00:53:05,910
Thailand?

1576
00:53:05,910 --> 00:53:09,090
(A familiar feeling)
Now I wanna go to Thailand again.

1577
00:53:09,150 --> 00:53:11,190
We could explore somewhere new.

1578
00:53:11,830 --> 00:53:14,590
First, let's go

1579
00:53:14,590 --> 00:53:15,630
to Disneyland.

1580
00:53:16,470 --> 00:53:19,070
Then Chongqing, right?

1581
00:53:19,070 --> 00:53:21,270
They're all on our list.

1582
00:53:21,270 --> 00:53:22,230
What else?

1583
00:53:22,230 --> 00:53:23,470
What else did we talk about?

1584
00:53:24,310 --> 00:53:25,790
So many things.

1585
00:53:25,790 --> 00:53:28,110
So many.

1586
00:53:28,260 --> 00:53:29,310
Roll down the window.

1587
00:53:29,310 --> 00:53:30,230
Look how pretty.

1588
00:53:31,590 --> 00:53:32,990
Beautiful.

1589
00:53:32,990 --> 00:53:34,230
It's gorgeous!

1590
00:53:35,670 --> 00:53:36,510
I'm sure

1591
00:53:36,510 --> 00:53:37,270
the restaurant we're going to

1592
00:53:37,270 --> 00:53:39,670
will have an amazing view too.

1593
00:53:42,430 --> 00:53:44,030
The mist makes it look even prettier.

1594
00:53:44,670 --> 00:53:45,230
So nice.

1595
00:53:45,230 --> 00:53:46,190
So beautiful.

1596
00:53:49,630 --> 00:53:50,710
Sheep!

1597
00:53:52,030 --> 00:53:52,870
Are those sheep?

1598
00:53:52,890 --> 00:53:53,650
Here.

1599
00:53:55,160 --> 00:53:56,670
Let's get some pictures of them.

1600
00:53:56,670 --> 00:53:57,550
I'll take some.

1601
00:53:57,790 --> 00:53:59,790
(Cao Yiheng's POV)
Look, that one's got curly hair.

1602
00:53:59,790 --> 00:54:01,430
(Naturally curly wool)
Just like your hair the other day.

1603
00:54:01,430 --> 00:54:02,630
They're even butting heads!

1604
00:54:04,460 --> 00:54:06,910
Bye-bye!

1605
00:54:07,570 --> 00:54:08,310
They're gone.

1606
00:54:08,310 --> 00:54:09,010
We're moving again.

1607
00:54:10,950 --> 00:54:11,830
We're here.

1608
00:54:11,830 --> 00:54:12,630
Let's get out.

1609
00:54:14,580 --> 00:54:15,890
It's so pretty inside.

1610
00:54:17,860 --> 00:54:18,700
Wow!

1611
00:54:19,520 --> 00:54:20,400
This is gorgeous.

1612
00:54:21,030 --> 00:54:22,470
How is it this pretty?

1613
00:54:22,470 --> 00:54:23,270
Yeah.

1614
00:54:24,070 --> 00:54:25,230
Thank you.

1615
00:54:25,230 --> 00:54:26,110
You're welcome.

1616
00:54:26,670 --> 00:54:27,870
That's a huge portion.

1617
00:54:27,870 --> 00:54:28,910
Thank you.

1618
00:54:30,250 --> 00:54:31,250
(Rubs hands together)

1619
00:54:31,530 --> 00:54:32,290
(Glances)

1620
00:54:32,390 --> 00:54:33,390
Why don't you sit over here?

1621
00:54:33,390 --> 00:54:33,910
Okay.

1622
00:54:35,350 --> 00:54:36,430
There's no wind on your side, right?

1623
00:54:36,430 --> 00:54:36,990
Yeah.

1624
00:54:36,990 --> 00:54:37,710
No wind over here.

1625
00:54:41,770 --> 00:54:42,410
(Checking on her)

1626
00:54:43,030 --> 00:54:43,510
Yeah.

1627
00:54:43,510 --> 00:54:44,450
It's warmer over here.

1628
00:54:47,150 --> 00:54:48,830
We finally got to try it today.

1629
00:54:49,630 --> 00:54:51,070
It was so much fun.

1630
00:54:51,070 --> 00:54:52,680
Sometimes it felt like free-falling.

1631
00:54:54,010 --> 00:54:55,660
And you drove really well.

1632
00:54:56,470 --> 00:54:57,750
(Can't hide his smile)
Not only were you a great driver,

1633
00:54:57,750 --> 00:54:58,790
you stayed so calm.

1634
00:54:58,790 --> 00:55:01,310
(Endless compliments)
And you made it really fun too.

1635
00:55:05,970 --> 00:55:07,370
(Hands it over)
Thanks.

1636
00:55:07,910 --> 00:55:08,710
Wanna do it again?

1637
00:55:08,710 --> 00:55:09,430
Definitely.

1638
00:55:09,430 --> 00:55:10,390
Next time, let's try...

1639
00:55:10,390 --> 00:55:11,270
A different course.

1640
00:55:11,270 --> 00:55:12,030
Yeah.

1641
00:55:12,590 --> 00:55:13,750
It was such a stress reliever.

1642
00:55:14,910 --> 00:55:15,750
Really?

1643
00:55:15,750 --> 00:55:17,110
Yeah, you don't have
to think about anything.

1644
00:55:17,110 --> 00:55:18,110
I could tell.

1645
00:55:18,110 --> 00:55:19,030
You were screaming the whole time.

1646
00:55:19,030 --> 00:55:20,190
And I didn't even have to drive.

1647
00:55:20,190 --> 00:55:21,830
My seat was the most relaxing.

1648
00:55:22,430 --> 00:55:23,790
I just had to enjoy the ride.

1649
00:55:24,870 --> 00:55:26,350
Have you been feeling stressed?

1650
00:55:26,990 --> 00:55:28,110
Not too much.

1651
00:55:28,110 --> 00:55:30,430
School just started,
and it's a new environment.

1652
00:55:30,430 --> 00:55:31,990
With this new major,

1653
00:55:31,990 --> 00:55:32,710
it's pretty stressful.

1654
00:55:32,710 --> 00:55:35,030
(Listening closely)

1655
00:55:35,030 --> 00:55:37,950
Do I seem stressed lately?

1656
00:55:37,950 --> 00:55:38,750
Not really, right?

1657
00:55:38,750 --> 00:55:41,430
Because when I need
to let my feelings out,

1658
00:55:41,430 --> 00:55:43,150
you're the only one I can vent to.

1659
00:55:43,150 --> 00:55:45,310
There's no one else who can handle

1660
00:55:45,310 --> 00:55:46,550
all my emotions.

1661
00:55:48,910 --> 00:55:49,950
Before, I could only sleep it off.

1662
00:55:49,950 --> 00:55:51,350
Now I can ramble to you too.

1663
00:55:52,230 --> 00:55:53,630
I think once you

1664
00:55:53,630 --> 00:55:55,030
get more familiar...

1665
00:55:56,230 --> 00:55:57,350
With my major...

1666
00:55:57,350 --> 00:55:58,590
And get the hang of things,

1667
00:55:58,590 --> 00:56:00,990
you won't feel as stressed.

1668
00:56:00,990 --> 00:56:03,150
It should get a little easier.

1669
00:56:04,260 --> 00:56:05,990
I've got another way to relax now.

1670
00:56:08,110 --> 00:56:09,550
Video calling you.

1671
00:56:11,110 --> 00:56:12,110
That helps you relax?

1672
00:56:12,110 --> 00:56:12,750
Yeah.

1673
00:56:12,750 --> 00:56:15,310
Say I've had a rough day.

1674
00:56:15,310 --> 00:56:16,990
I answer a video call and see

1675
00:56:16,990 --> 00:56:18,310
a handsome face.

1676
00:56:18,310 --> 00:56:19,270
Instant stress relief.

1677
00:56:22,910 --> 00:56:23,870
When I'm stressed,

1678
00:56:23,870 --> 00:56:26,950
I only open up to people
I'm really close to.

1679
00:56:26,950 --> 00:56:29,550
How close is close enough for you?

1680
00:56:29,550 --> 00:56:30,470
You count.

1681
00:56:32,550 --> 00:56:33,630
Having you around...

1682
00:56:33,630 --> 00:56:35,390
After I talk things through with you,

1683
00:56:35,390 --> 00:56:36,430
I feel better faster.

1684
00:56:37,590 --> 00:56:38,950
When you talk things through with me,

1685
00:56:38,950 --> 00:56:40,110
somehow you just

1686
00:56:40,110 --> 00:56:41,150
make it impossible to stay mad.

1687
00:56:41,150 --> 00:56:41,770
Why's that?

1688
00:56:41,770 --> 00:56:42,350
(Tell me)

1689
00:56:42,350 --> 00:56:43,110
Why is that?

1690
00:56:45,310 --> 00:56:46,470
If I just lectured you,

1691
00:56:46,470 --> 00:56:48,590
wouldn't I only be focusing

1692
00:56:48,590 --> 00:56:50,750
on who's right or wrong?

1693
00:56:50,750 --> 00:56:51,730
And what kind

1694
00:56:51,740 --> 00:56:54,390
of relationship would that be?

1695
00:56:58,390 --> 00:57:00,510
You're so much more outgoing now.

1696
00:57:00,510 --> 00:57:02,390
Aren't you the one who keeps texting me

1697
00:57:02,390 --> 00:57:03,230
to be more cheerful

1698
00:57:03,230 --> 00:57:03,910
and more expressive?

1699
00:57:06,350 --> 00:57:07,310
It's a good thing.

1700
00:57:09,910 --> 00:57:10,510
So

1701
00:57:10,510 --> 00:57:12,070
have you found your rhythm yet?

1702
00:57:12,070 --> 00:57:12,870
Like...

1703
00:57:12,870 --> 00:57:14,510
I haven't quite found it yet.

1704
00:57:14,510 --> 00:57:15,950
I think it just takes...

1705
00:57:18,110 --> 00:57:19,390
You can't expect

1706
00:57:19,390 --> 00:57:21,590
to know everything right away.

1707
00:57:22,270 --> 00:57:23,910
You just have to adjust gradually.

1708
00:57:24,550 --> 00:57:25,830
So for me,

1709
00:57:25,830 --> 00:57:26,870
I'm doing okay.

1710
00:57:27,150 --> 00:57:30,550
And your field takes time

1711
00:57:30,550 --> 00:57:31,110
to really master.

1712
00:57:31,830 --> 00:57:32,150
Yeah.

1713
00:57:32,630 --> 00:57:34,870
But I think

1714
00:57:34,870 --> 00:57:35,870
with my lab work,

1715
00:57:35,870 --> 00:57:37,350
my professors and senior students say

1716
00:57:37,350 --> 00:57:38,830
it's really just about

1717
00:57:38,830 --> 00:57:40,910
learning through repetition.

1718
00:57:41,830 --> 00:57:42,790
As long as you work hard,

1719
00:57:42,790 --> 00:57:43,750
you can make it

1720
00:57:43,750 --> 00:57:44,750
halfway up the mountain,

1721
00:57:44,750 --> 00:57:46,030
or even 70% of the way.

1722
00:57:46,810 --> 00:57:48,150
You might not reach the top,

1723
00:57:48,150 --> 00:57:49,190
but if you don't try,

1724
00:57:49,190 --> 00:57:50,750
you'll stay at the bottom.

1725
00:57:50,750 --> 00:57:51,530
(Hard work gets you halfway up)

1726
00:57:51,530 --> 00:57:52,370
(Without effort,
you're stuck at the bottom)

1727
00:57:54,470 --> 00:57:55,990
I think if you've made it halfway

1728
00:57:55,990 --> 00:57:56,750
or even

1729
00:57:56,750 --> 00:57:57,870
70% of the way up,

1730
00:57:58,110 --> 00:57:59,990
you've already seen 70% of the view.

1731
00:57:59,990 --> 00:58:01,590
I'd call that a success.

1732
00:58:05,510 --> 00:58:06,910
Maybe only those
with talent and dedication

1733
00:58:06,910 --> 00:58:08,030
can reach the summit.

1734
00:58:08,950 --> 00:58:10,510
Everyone has their own summit.

1735
00:58:10,650 --> 00:58:12,150
(Everyone has their own summit)

1736
00:58:12,150 --> 00:58:12,670
Exactly.

1737
00:58:13,270 --> 00:58:14,510
There's no need
to make someone else's goals

1738
00:58:14,510 --> 00:58:15,590
your own.

1739
00:58:16,380 --> 00:58:16,990
True.

1740
00:58:21,040 --> 00:58:22,150
But I think

1741
00:58:22,150 --> 00:58:24,390
studying medicine is really tough.

1742
00:58:25,630 --> 00:58:26,990
Like when I studied nursing,

1743
00:58:27,130 --> 00:58:29,230
the instructors at the hospital

1744
00:58:29,230 --> 00:58:30,310
worked incredibly hard.

1745
00:58:30,310 --> 00:58:31,390
They even worked night shifts.

1746
00:58:31,950 --> 00:58:32,990
And they

1747
00:58:32,990 --> 00:58:34,150
have so much

1748
00:58:34,150 --> 00:58:35,550
to worry about at the hospital.

1749
00:58:36,630 --> 00:58:38,350
Doctors often work 24-hour shifts.

1750
00:58:38,790 --> 00:58:40,270
They're there all day.

1751
00:58:41,390 --> 00:58:43,030
And when you're at the hospital,

1752
00:58:43,030 --> 00:58:44,870
you can never fully relax.

1753
00:58:45,190 --> 00:58:46,190
For example,

1754
00:58:46,190 --> 00:58:47,150
even when there's nothing happening,

1755
00:58:47,150 --> 00:58:49,430
your mind can't switch off.

1756
00:58:49,790 --> 00:58:51,470
Because an emergency

1757
00:58:51,470 --> 00:58:52,630
could happen anytime.

1758
00:58:52,630 --> 00:58:53,790
You have

1759
00:58:53,790 --> 00:58:55,270
to stay alert at all times.

1760
00:58:56,950 --> 00:58:57,790
Anyway, I think

1761
00:58:57,790 --> 00:59:00,230
working in our university's lab

1762
00:59:00,670 --> 00:59:01,990
or doing research

1763
00:59:02,790 --> 00:59:03,990
is also really demanding.

1764
00:59:03,990 --> 00:59:05,230
There's so much repetition.

1765
00:59:05,230 --> 00:59:06,670
And it requires

1766
00:59:06,670 --> 00:59:09,190
patience
and a rigorous scientific mindset.

1767
00:59:10,110 --> 00:59:10,990
It's pretty tough.

1768
00:59:11,870 --> 00:59:12,590
What about you?

1769
00:59:12,590 --> 00:59:14,670
I feel like drawing
takes a lot of talent.

1770
00:59:14,910 --> 00:59:16,190
Not necessarily.

1771
00:59:16,190 --> 00:59:16,950
It's also

1772
00:59:16,950 --> 00:59:17,870
pretty much the same.

1773
00:59:17,870 --> 00:59:18,430
Pretty much.

1774
00:59:18,430 --> 00:59:19,310
There's really

1775
00:59:19,310 --> 00:59:20,830
nothing hard work can't achieve.

1776
00:59:20,830 --> 00:59:21,550
I think.

1777
00:59:24,710 --> 00:59:25,910
It's just a matter of time.

1778
00:59:25,910 --> 00:59:27,990
Can hard work
improve your sense of style?

1779
00:59:27,990 --> 00:59:29,830
Like your fashion sense and stuff?

1780
00:59:30,590 --> 00:59:31,830
(Curious)
Of course.

1781
00:59:31,830 --> 00:59:33,350
It's not like

1782
00:59:33,350 --> 00:59:34,550
you're born with great style.

1783
00:59:35,030 --> 00:59:37,350
For a lot of people,

1784
00:59:37,350 --> 00:59:38,510
as they get older,

1785
00:59:39,030 --> 00:59:40,030
their fashion sense

1786
00:59:40,030 --> 00:59:41,150
gets better and better.

1787
00:59:41,150 --> 00:59:41,950
Yeah.

1788
00:59:47,990 --> 00:59:49,950
When did you paint with oils?

1789
00:59:49,950 --> 00:59:50,710
Like these.

1790
00:59:51,110 --> 00:59:52,150
In college.

1791
00:59:52,150 --> 00:59:52,950
College?

1792
00:59:53,750 --> 00:59:54,750
Did you paint a lot?

1793
00:59:54,750 --> 00:59:55,550
Not much.

1794
00:59:57,080 --> 00:59:58,150
But I've seen your paintings.

1795
00:59:58,150 --> 00:59:59,150
A lot of them

1796
00:59:59,150 --> 01:00:00,510
looked like

1797
01:00:00,510 --> 01:00:01,870
they were done digitally.

1798
01:00:02,040 --> 01:00:02,770
What kind of paintings are those?

1799
01:00:02,770 --> 01:00:03,450
(Curious)

1800
01:00:03,630 --> 01:00:04,430
Acrylics.

1801
01:00:04,910 --> 01:00:05,510
Acrylics?

1802
01:00:05,510 --> 01:00:06,470
Yeah, acrylic paintings.

1803
01:00:06,750 --> 01:00:08,630
Does it feel different to paint with?

1804
01:00:08,630 --> 01:00:09,390
Not really.

1805
01:00:09,390 --> 01:00:10,710
It just dries faster.

1806
01:00:11,430 --> 01:00:13,750
Do the finished paintings look similar?

1807
01:00:14,130 --> 01:00:16,190
(Curious)
Oil paintings are more

1808
01:00:16,470 --> 01:00:17,270
translucent.

1809
01:00:18,750 --> 01:00:20,030
Is that an oil painting up there too?

1810
01:00:20,030 --> 01:00:21,350
It looks so detailed.

1811
01:00:21,350 --> 01:00:22,390
Realistic oil painting.

1812
01:00:22,390 --> 01:00:23,910
I saw the signature at the bottom right.

1813
01:00:24,510 --> 01:00:25,950
I think they're all signed.

1814
01:00:26,630 --> 01:00:27,790
Do you

1815
01:00:27,790 --> 01:00:29,350
sign your paintings?

1816
01:00:29,710 --> 01:00:30,310
No.

1817
01:00:31,150 --> 01:00:32,590
I remember in first grade,

1818
01:00:32,590 --> 01:00:33,590
I'd sign all my drawings.

1819
01:00:35,630 --> 01:00:36,750
That's fine too.

1820
01:00:36,750 --> 01:00:38,870
My paintings are just too big.

1821
01:00:38,870 --> 01:00:39,830
They're huge.

1822
01:00:39,830 --> 01:00:41,390
This one's pretty big too.

1823
01:00:45,510 --> 01:00:47,510
And when you paint

1824
01:00:47,510 --> 01:00:49,270
murals, it's hard to sign them, right?

1825
01:00:50,070 --> 01:00:51,230
You don't sign murals.

1826
01:00:51,230 --> 01:00:51,870
Yeah.

1827
01:00:56,230 --> 01:00:57,550
The holidays are coming.

1828
01:00:57,950 --> 01:00:58,710
The National Day holiday.

1829
01:00:58,710 --> 01:00:59,230
Mid-Autumn Festival.

1830
01:00:59,230 --> 01:01:00,630
I think Mid-Autumn comes first.

1831
01:01:00,630 --> 01:01:01,170
Yeah.

1832
01:01:02,390 --> 01:01:04,150
So, for Mid-Autumn Festival...

1833
01:01:06,630 --> 01:01:07,870
would you like

1834
01:01:07,870 --> 01:01:08,910
to meet my parents?

1835
01:01:09,010 --> 01:01:10,650
(Sits up straight)

1836
01:01:13,270 --> 01:01:14,070
Sure.

1837
01:01:18,470 --> 01:01:21,270
We could have dinner together.

1838
01:01:22,130 --> 01:01:23,270
My dad

1839
01:01:23,270 --> 01:01:24,910
definitely won't let you off

1840
01:01:24,910 --> 01:01:25,790
with just dinner.

1841
01:01:27,530 --> 01:01:28,610
(Sits up straight)

1842
01:01:31,830 --> 01:01:33,390
Are you nervous about meeting them?

1843
01:01:33,850 --> 01:01:34,850
(Already getting nervous)

1844
01:01:38,230 --> 01:01:40,030
Do you think it's the right time?

1845
01:01:40,760 --> 01:01:42,240
Mid-Autumn Festival
is such a special day.

1846
01:01:44,680 --> 01:01:46,070
I think having dinner would be nice.

1847
01:01:46,070 --> 01:01:47,470
It has a pretty nice meaning.

1848
01:01:48,070 --> 01:01:49,150
I mean...

1849
01:01:49,150 --> 01:01:50,830
How do I put it?

1850
01:01:50,830 --> 01:01:51,950
Well...

1851
01:01:55,000 --> 01:01:55,650
Meaningful.

1852
01:01:56,510 --> 01:01:57,670
I think it's really meaningful.

1853
01:01:57,670 --> 01:01:58,530
Mid-Autumn Festival.

1854
01:01:59,120 --> 01:02:00,710
I bet my parents will be nervous too.

1855
01:02:02,750 --> 01:02:05,190
Anyway, my parents are really nice.

1856
01:02:05,190 --> 01:02:06,190
Don't worry.

1857
01:02:06,190 --> 01:02:07,350
Don't be nervous.

1858
01:02:07,350 --> 01:02:08,670
I'm not nervous.

1859
01:02:12,510 --> 01:02:13,510
Why are you...

1860
01:02:15,670 --> 01:02:17,150
Ever since my dad saw us on the show,

1861
01:02:17,150 --> 01:02:18,990
he's wanted to sing with you.

1862
01:02:20,690 --> 01:02:22,270
(Takes a sip of tea)

1863
01:02:22,270 --> 01:02:24,750
He wants to have a sing-off with you.

1864
01:02:27,350 --> 01:02:28,510
Then later,

1865
01:02:28,510 --> 01:02:30,420
you'll have to make me a list.

1866
01:02:30,420 --> 01:02:31,780
What were those songs?

1867
01:02:31,780 --> 01:02:33,350
Sailor.

1868
01:02:33,350 --> 01:02:34,150
(Well)
And what was that other one?

1869
01:02:34,150 --> 01:02:35,590
999 Roses.

1870
01:02:35,590 --> 01:02:37,270
He's sung those since I was little.

1871
01:02:37,270 --> 01:02:38,910
But you can't sing better than my dad.

1872
01:02:40,590 --> 01:02:41,710
He's a little petty.

1873
01:02:42,030 --> 01:02:42,870
If you outsing him,

1874
01:02:42,870 --> 01:02:44,750
(Joking)
he'll put you on his blacklist.

1875
01:02:48,070 --> 01:02:49,150
What about your mom?

1876
01:02:49,670 --> 01:02:50,330
She's a lot like me.

1877
01:02:50,330 --> 01:02:51,750
She likes

1878
01:02:51,750 --> 01:02:53,230
watching TV

1879
01:02:53,470 --> 01:02:55,480
and just relaxing.

1880
01:02:56,470 --> 01:02:58,310
My dad has three favorite things.

1881
01:02:58,310 --> 01:03:00,590
Singing,

1882
01:03:00,590 --> 01:03:02,150
having a drink,

1883
01:03:02,900 --> 01:03:03,630
and soccer.

1884
01:03:03,890 --> 01:03:04,890
(Taking mental notes)

1885
01:03:04,890 --> 01:03:06,630
My dad absolutely loves playing soccer.

1886
01:03:06,830 --> 01:03:07,990
And watching it too.

1887
01:03:08,910 --> 01:03:09,990
And when I was little,

1888
01:03:09,990 --> 01:03:11,750
in first or second grade...

1889
01:03:12,230 --> 01:03:13,550
I think it was first grade.

1890
01:03:13,830 --> 01:03:15,260
He insisted I learn soccer.

1891
01:03:17,710 --> 01:03:18,550
And then...

1892
01:03:18,790 --> 01:03:19,390
You know what?

1893
01:03:19,390 --> 01:03:20,310
When you did

1894
01:03:20,310 --> 01:03:21,270
that magazine shoot,

1895
01:03:21,270 --> 01:03:23,030
you really looked like a soccer player.

1896
01:03:23,030 --> 01:03:24,310
Oh, come on!

1897
01:03:27,150 --> 01:03:28,590
So how good did you get?

1898
01:03:28,910 --> 01:03:29,870
How good?

1899
01:03:29,870 --> 01:03:31,910
I learned what a soccer ball was.

1900
01:03:31,910 --> 01:03:33,090
(Total beginner)

1901
01:03:35,070 --> 01:03:36,230
If your dad loves soccer,

1902
01:03:36,230 --> 01:03:38,190
he must watch the World Cup, right?

1903
01:03:38,190 --> 01:03:38,990
He does.

1904
01:03:39,430 --> 01:03:41,270
Does he predict which team will win?

1905
01:03:41,550 --> 01:03:42,630
He used to.

1906
01:03:43,090 --> 01:03:43,990
He makes predictions.

1907
01:03:44,340 --> 01:03:45,150
And then

1908
01:03:45,150 --> 01:03:47,110
whenever there's a match,

1909
01:03:47,110 --> 01:03:47,870
I can't...

1910
01:03:47,870 --> 01:03:49,430
He'd hog the TV.

1911
01:03:49,710 --> 01:03:50,510
I can't watch anything.

1912
01:03:50,840 --> 01:03:51,950
It's all his.

1913
01:03:54,630 --> 01:03:56,630
When we first entered
the house this year,

1914
01:03:56,630 --> 01:03:57,950
the World Cup had just started.

1915
01:03:57,950 --> 01:03:58,550
So was your dad...

1916
01:03:58,550 --> 01:03:59,870
He was definitely watching.

1917
01:03:59,870 --> 01:04:02,670
Every single day.

1918
01:04:02,670 --> 01:04:03,670
Every day.

1919
01:04:03,670 --> 01:04:04,590
Right on schedule.

1920
01:04:05,510 --> 01:04:06,910
What about your parents?

1921
01:04:08,070 --> 01:04:10,750
They used to love

1922
01:04:10,750 --> 01:04:11,870
traveling.

1923
01:04:12,710 --> 01:04:13,510
And they also

1924
01:04:13,510 --> 01:04:15,110
enjoy having a drink.

1925
01:04:15,970 --> 01:04:17,050
(Something in common)

1926
01:04:21,740 --> 01:04:22,980
What does your dad like to eat?

1927
01:04:23,190 --> 01:04:24,910
He eats pretty much anything.

1928
01:04:24,910 --> 01:04:27,290
But neither of us eats lamb.

1929
01:04:27,290 --> 01:04:29,570
(Quietly taking notes)

1930
01:04:30,030 --> 01:04:30,750
Between your parents,

1931
01:04:30,750 --> 01:04:31,870
who do you look more like?

1932
01:04:33,190 --> 01:04:34,670
A bit of both.

1933
01:04:35,190 --> 01:04:35,910
It's pretty obvious.

1934
01:04:35,910 --> 01:04:36,390
I think.

1935
01:04:36,390 --> 01:04:37,030
Really?

1936
01:04:37,630 --> 01:04:38,590
I'll probably see it.

1937
01:04:39,070 --> 01:04:41,030
My parents say I got
their best features.

1938
01:04:41,030 --> 01:04:42,190
So I don't look like either of them.

1939
01:04:43,550 --> 01:04:44,630
My dad's put on weight now.

1940
01:04:44,630 --> 01:04:45,630
He used to be really skinny.

1941
01:04:45,630 --> 01:04:46,390
Didn't I show you

1942
01:04:46,390 --> 01:04:48,350
photos of my parents
when they were young?

1943
01:04:48,350 --> 01:04:48,990
I remember.

1944
01:04:48,990 --> 01:04:49,830
They look familiar.

1945
01:04:49,920 --> 01:04:51,790
You three aren't just gonna sit there

1946
01:04:51,790 --> 01:04:52,630
smiling awkwardly at Mid-Autumn, right?

1947
01:04:52,630 --> 01:04:53,990
Leaving me to do all the talking?

1948
01:04:56,280 --> 01:04:57,840
I just want your parents

1949
01:04:57,850 --> 01:04:59,010
to get to know me better.

1950
01:04:59,010 --> 01:04:59,600
Yeah.

1951
01:04:59,720 --> 01:05:00,330
That kind of thing.

1952
01:05:00,330 --> 01:05:01,710
They already know you pretty well.

1953
01:05:03,230 --> 01:05:05,630
My parents have actually mentioned you.

1954
01:05:06,110 --> 01:05:06,870
I mean...

1955
01:05:06,870 --> 01:05:07,950
They watch you frame by frame.

1956
01:05:09,350 --> 01:05:11,270
Even more closely than they watch me.

1957
01:05:19,870 --> 01:05:22,390
Then I'd better start preparing.

1958
01:05:22,390 --> 01:05:23,230
Don't worry.

1959
01:05:23,230 --> 01:05:23,990
Don't be nervous.

1960
01:05:25,530 --> 01:05:26,530
(Next episode)

1961
01:05:26,550 --> 01:05:26,950
Cao Yiheng.

1962
01:05:27,190 --> 01:05:27,990
Hello, sir. Hello, ma'am.

1963
01:05:27,990 --> 01:05:28,430
Hello.

1964
01:05:28,950 --> 01:05:29,790
You two look so young.

1965
01:05:29,790 --> 01:05:30,830
You're so slim.

1966
01:05:32,150 --> 01:05:33,750
He said he'd act all serious.

1967
01:05:33,750 --> 01:05:35,030
But he cracked the moment you walked in.

1968
01:05:35,710 --> 01:05:36,630
I'm pretty serious.

1969
01:05:37,590 --> 01:05:39,430
(Asking questions)
How's your mural work going?

1970
01:05:39,430 --> 01:05:41,230
(Asking questions)
Does anyone in your family work in art?

1971
01:05:41,230 --> 01:05:42,470
(Asking questions)
What are Cui Kaiyi's flaws?

1972
01:05:42,470 --> 01:05:44,110
Are you independent?

1973
01:05:47,790 --> 01:05:48,670
(Compliments)
You're that good?

1974
01:05:48,670 --> 01:05:49,790
See, if you do it like this,

1975
01:05:49,790 --> 01:05:50,990
(Sharing some tips)
you'll be more accurate.

1976
01:05:50,990 --> 01:05:51,470
Like this.

1977
01:05:52,090 --> 01:05:52,810
(Nailed the pose)

1978
01:05:54,790 --> 01:05:55,510
There you go.

1979
01:05:55,510 --> 01:05:56,510
Learned from the best.

1980
01:05:58,290 --> 01:05:59,890
(Getting mischievous)

1981
01:05:59,970 --> 01:06:00,770
You're so annoying!

1982
01:06:06,870 --> 01:06:08,470
Let's start the game.

1983
01:06:08,470 --> 01:06:08,910
Okay.

1984
01:06:08,910 --> 01:06:09,510
Let's go!

1985
01:06:09,710 --> 01:06:11,370
One, two! One, two!

1986
01:06:11,370 --> 01:06:12,210
(Full of energy)
One, two!

1987
01:06:12,210 --> 01:06:13,270
(Moving like lightning)
One, two!

1988
01:06:13,270 --> 01:06:14,110
Cao Yiheng, take bigger steps.

1989
01:06:14,110 --> 01:06:14,670
Cao Yiheng.

1990
01:06:14,670 --> 01:06:15,590
One, two! One, two!

1991
01:06:15,910 --> 01:06:17,710
This is a piece of cake, guys!

1992
01:06:17,770 --> 01:06:18,450
(Falls over)

1993
01:06:19,270 --> 01:06:20,470
Whoever unties it first gets it!

1994
01:06:21,430 --> 01:06:22,630
That's not how you play!

1995
01:06:24,750 --> 01:06:25,590
Come on!

1996
01:06:25,590 --> 01:06:26,350
Cheers!

1997
01:06:26,350 --> 01:06:27,510
What a great time!

1998
01:06:27,630 --> 01:06:29,870
Let's get together again soon!

1999
01:06:44,500 --> 01:06:47,220
♪Morning steam rises
from breakfast stalls♪

2000
01:06:47,220 --> 01:06:49,820
♪Packed subway cars,
barely room to breathe♪

2001
01:06:49,820 --> 01:06:54,020
♪Still half asleep, another day begins♪

2002
01:06:55,180 --> 01:06:57,900
♪The city glows beneath the towers♪

2003
01:06:57,900 --> 01:07:00,540
♪Somewhere beyond the clouds,
a sweet little date awaits♪

2004
01:07:00,540 --> 01:07:04,620
♪But first,
there are endless meetings to survive♪

2005
01:07:05,340 --> 01:07:06,740
♪Even if the fairy tale
only lasts a day♪

2006
01:07:06,740 --> 01:07:08,060
♪I'll still give it everything I have♪

2007
01:07:08,060 --> 01:07:09,380
♪Love out loud♪

2008
01:07:09,380 --> 01:07:10,780
♪Don't let this summer slip away♪

2009
01:07:10,780 --> 01:07:12,020
♪Cupid's arrow is already on its way♪

2010
01:07:12,020 --> 01:07:13,420
♪Don't act like you didn't see it♪

2011
01:07:13,420 --> 01:07:16,380
♪Just be a little braver♪

2012
01:07:16,380 --> 01:07:19,220
♪Keep moving♪

2013
01:07:19,220 --> 01:07:22,580
♪There's a little spark shining
in your eyes♪

2014
01:07:24,940 --> 01:07:27,300
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

2015
01:07:37,740 --> 01:07:40,540
♪Keep moving♪

2016
01:07:40,540 --> 01:07:43,180
♪Life can be complicated,
yet beautifully simple♪

2017
01:07:43,180 --> 01:07:45,820
♪Go discover♪

2018
01:07:45,820 --> 01:07:48,500
♪That heartbeat you've been longing
to let out♪

2019
01:07:48,500 --> 01:07:51,180
♪Come closer♪

2020
01:07:51,180 --> 01:07:54,580
♪There's a little spark shining
in your eyes♪

2021
01:07:57,020 --> 01:07:59,820
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪
